            {
              "text": "(rarely useful).",
              "style": "Plain"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Note the documentation for the primitives ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "str",
              "style": "InlineCode",
              "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.str.html"
            },
            {
              "text": " and ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "[T]",
              "style": "InlineCode",
              "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.slice.html"
            },
            {
              "text": " (also",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "called 'slice'). Many method calls on ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "String",
              "style": "InlineCode",
              "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/string/index.html?search=alloc%3A%3Astring%3A%3AString"
            },
            {
              "text": " and ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "Vec<T>",
              "style": "InlineCode",
              "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/index.html?search=alloc%3A%3Avec%3A%3AVec"
            },
            {
              "text": " are actually",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "calls to methods on ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "str",
              "style": "InlineCode",
              "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.str.html"
            },
            {
              "text": " and ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "[T]",
              "style": "InlineCode",
              "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.slice.html"
            },
            {
              "text": " respectively, via ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "deref",
              "style": "Plain",
              "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/index.html?search=std%3A%3A%2E%2Fbook%2Fch15%2D02%2Dderef"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain",
              "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/index.html?search=std%3A%3A%2E%2Fbook%2Fch15%2D02%2Dderef"
            },
            {
              "text": "coercions",
              "style": "Plain",
              "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/index.html?search=std%3A%3A%2E%2Fbook%2Fch15%2D02%2Dderef"
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "style": "Plain"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Third, the standard library defines ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "The Rust Prelude",
              "style": "Plain",
              "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/prelude/index.html"
            },
            {
              "text": ", a small collection",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "of items - mostly traits - that are imported into every module of every",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "crate. The traits in the prelude are pervasive, making the prelude",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "documentation a good entry point to learning about the library.",
              "style": "Plain"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "And finally, the standard library exports a number of standard macros, and",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "lists them on this page",
              "style": "Plain",
              "url": "#macros"
            },
            {
              "text": " (technically, not all of the standard",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "macros are defined by the standard library - some are defined by the",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "compiler - but they are documented here the same). Like the prelude, the",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "standard macros are imported by default into all crates.",
              "style": "Plain"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": "Title",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Contributing changes to the documentation",
              "style": "Plain"
