              "text": ".",
              "style": "Plain"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": "Section",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Platform abstractions and I/O",
              "style": "Plain"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Besides basic data types, the standard library is largely concerned with",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "abstracting over differences in common platforms, most notably Windows and",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "Unix derivatives.",
              "style": "Plain"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Common types of I/O, including ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "files",
              "style": "Plain",
              "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/fs/struct.File.html"
            },
            {
              "text": ", ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "TCP",
              "style": "Plain",
              "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/net/tcp/struct.TcpStream.html"
            },
            {
              "text": ", and ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "UDP",
              "style": "Plain",
              "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/net/udp/struct.UdpSocket.html"
            },
            {
              "text": ", are defined in",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "the ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "io",
              "style": "InlineCode",
              "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/io/index.html"
            },
            {
              "text": ", ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "fs",
              "style": "InlineCode",
              "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/fs/index.html"
            },
            {
              "text": ", and ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "net",
              "style": "InlineCode",
              "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/net/index.html"
            },
            {
              "text": " modules.",
              "style": "Plain"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "thread",
              "style": "InlineCode",
              "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/thread/index.html"
            },
            {
              "text": " module contains Rust's threading abstractions. ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "sync",
              "style": "InlineCode",
              "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/sync/index.html"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "contains further primitive shared memory types, including ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "atomic",
              "style": "InlineCode",
              "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/sync/index.html?search=core%3A%3Async%3A%3Aatomic"
            },
            {
              "text": ", ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "mpmc",
              "style": "InlineCode",
              "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/sync/mpmc/index.html"
            },
            {
              "text": " and",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "mpsc",
              "style": "InlineCode",
              "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/sync/mpsc/index.html"
            },
            {
              "text": ", which contains the channel types for message passing.",
              "style": "Plain"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": "Title",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Use before and after ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "main()",
              "style": "InlineCode"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Many parts of the standard library are expected to work before and after ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "main()",
              "style": "InlineCode"
            },
            {
              "text": ";",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "but this is not guaranteed or ensured by tests. It is recommended that you write your own tests",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "and run them on each platform you wish to support.",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "This means that use of ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "std",
              "style": "InlineCode"
            },
            {
              "text": " before/after main, especially of features that interact with the",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "OS or global state, is exempted from stability and portability guarantees and instead only",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "provided on a best-effort basis. Nevertheless bug reports are appreciated.",
              "style": "Plain"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "On the other hand ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "core",
              "style": "InlineCode"
            },
            {
              "text": " and ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "alloc",
              "style": "InlineCode"
            },
            {
              "text": " are most likely to work in such environments with",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "the caveat that any hookable behavior such as panics, oom handling or allocators will also",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "depend on the compatibility of the hooks.",
              "style": "Plain"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Some features may also behave differently outside main, e.g. stdio could become unbuffered,",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "some panics might turn into aborts, backtraces might not get symbolicated or similar.",
              "style": "Plain"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Non-exhaustive list of known limitations:",
              "style": "Plain"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            {
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "after-main use of thread-locals, which also affects additional features:",
                      "style": "Plain"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "spans": [
                            {
                              "text": "thread::current()",
                              "style": "InlineCode",
                              "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/thread/current/fn.current.html"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "under UNIX, before main, file descriptors 0, 1, and 2 may be unchanged",
                      "style": "Plain"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": " ",
                      "style": "Plain"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "(they are guaranteed to be open during main,",
                      "style": "Plain"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": " ",
                      "style": "Plain"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "and are opened to /dev/null O_RDWR if they weren't open on program start)",
                      "style": "Plain"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "level": "Full"
    }
  ],
  "body": {
    "kind": "module",
    "items": [
      {
        "path": "prelude",
        "kind": "module",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/prelude/index.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The Rust Prelude",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Rust comes with a variety of things in its standard library. However, if",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "you had to manually import every single thing that you used, it would be",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "very verbose. But importing a lot of things that a program never uses isn't",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "good either. A balance needs to be struck.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "prelude",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is the list of things that Rust automatically imports into",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "every Rust program. It's kept as small as possible, and is focused on",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "things, particularly traits, which are used in almost every single Rust",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "program.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Other preludes",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Preludes can be seen as a pattern to make using multiple types more",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "convenient. As such, you'll find other preludes in the standard library,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "such as ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "std::io::prelude",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/io/prelude/index.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". Various libraries in the Rust ecosystem may",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "also define their own preludes.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The difference between 'the prelude' and these other preludes is that they",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "are not automatically ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "use",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "'d, and must be imported manually. This is still",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "easier than importing all of their constituent components.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
