      {
        "path": "thread",
        "kind": "module",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/thread/index.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Native threads.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The threading model",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "An executing Rust program consists of a collection of native OS threads,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "each with their own stack and local state. Threads can be named, and",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "provide some built-in support for low-level synchronization.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Communication between threads can be done through",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "channels",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/sync/mpsc/index.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", Rust's message-passing types, along with ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "other forms of thread",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/../../std/index.html?search=std%3A%3A%2E%2E%3A%3A%2E%2E%3A%3Astd%3A%3Async"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/../../std/index.html?search=std%3A%3A%2E%2E%3A%3A%2E%2E%3A%3Astd%3A%3Async"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "synchronization",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/../../std/index.html?search=std%3A%3A%2E%2E%3A%3A%2E%2E%3A%3Astd%3A%3Async"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and shared-memory data",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "structures. In particular, types that are guaranteed to be",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "threadsafe are easily shared between threads using the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "atomically-reference-counted container, ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Arc",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/sync/index.html?search=alloc%3A%3Async%3A%3AArc"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Fatal logic errors in Rust cause ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "thread panic",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", during which",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "a thread will unwind the stack, running destructors and freeing",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "owned resources. While not meant as a 'try/catch' mechanism, panics",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "in Rust can nonetheless be caught (unless compiling with ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "panic=abort",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ") with",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "catch_unwind",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/index.html?search=std%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fstd%2Fpanic%2Ffn%2Ecatch%5Funwind"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and recovered",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "from, or alternatively be resumed with",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "resume_unwind",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/index.html?search=std%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fstd%2Fpanic%2Ffn%2Eresume%5Funwind"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". If the panic",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "is not caught the thread will exit, but the panic may optionally be",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "detected from a different thread with ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "join",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/thread/join_handle/struct.JoinHandle.html#method.join"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". If the main thread panics",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "without the panic being caught, the application will exit with a",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "non-zero exit code.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "When the main thread of a Rust program terminates, the entire program shuts",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "down, even if other threads are still running, and any destructors on the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "remaining threads' stacks may not be executed.  However, this module",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "provides convenient facilities for automatically waiting for the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "termination of a thread (i.e., join).",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Spawning a thread",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "A new thread can be spawned using the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "thread::spawn",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/thread/functions/fn.spawn.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " function:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "use std::thread;\n\nthread::spawn(move || {\n    // some work here\n});"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "In this example, the spawned thread is \"detached,\" which means that there is",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "no way for the program to learn when the spawned thread completes or otherwise",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "terminates.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "To learn when a thread completes, it is necessary to capture the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "JoinHandle",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/thread/join_handle/struct.JoinHandle.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "object that is returned by the call to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "spawn",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/thread/functions/fn.spawn.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", which provides",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "join",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " method that allows the caller to wait for the completion of the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "spawned thread:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "use std::thread;\n\nlet thread_join_handle = thread::spawn(move || {\n    // some work here\n});\n// some work here\nlet res = thread_join_handle.join();"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "join",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/thread/join_handle/struct.JoinHandle.html#method.join"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " method returns a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "thread::Result",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/thread/type.Result.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " containing ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Ok",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/result/Result/index.html?search=core%3A%3Aresult%3A%3AResult%3A%3AOk"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " of the final",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "value produced by the spawned thread, or ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Err",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/result/Result/index.html?search=core%3A%3Aresult%3A%3AResult%3A%3AErr"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " of the value given to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "a call to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "panic!",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/macro.panic.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " if the thread panicked.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Note that there is no parent/child relationship between a thread that spawns a",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "new thread and the thread being spawned.  In particular, the spawned thread may or",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "may not outlive the spawning thread, unless the spawning thread is the main thread.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Configuring threads",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "A new thread can be configured before it is spawned via the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Builder",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/thread/builder/struct.Builder.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " type,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
