                  },
                  {
                    "text": "by the APIs of this module.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Thread-local storage",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This module also provides an implementation of thread-local storage for Rust",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "programs. Thread-local storage is a method of storing data into a global",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "variable that each thread in the program will have its own copy of.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Threads do not share this data, so accesses do not need to be synchronized.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "A thread-local key owns the value it contains and will destroy the value when the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "thread exits. It is created with the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "thread_local!",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/macro.thread_local.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " macro and can contain any",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "value that is ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "'static",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " (no borrowed pointers). It provides an accessor function,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "with",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/thread/local/struct.LocalKey.html#method.with"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", that yields a shared reference to the value to the specified",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "closure. Thread-local keys allow only shared access to values, as there would be no",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "way to guarantee uniqueness if mutable borrows were allowed. Most values",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "will want to make use of some form of ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "interior mutability",
                    "style": "Strong"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " through the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cell",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cell/index.html?search=core%3A%3Acell%3A%3ACell"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " or ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "RefCell",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cell/index.html?search=core%3A%3Acell%3A%3ARefCell"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " types.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Naming threads",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Threads are able to have associated names for identification purposes. By default, spawned",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "threads are unnamed. To specify a name for a thread, build the thread with ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Builder",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/thread/builder/struct.Builder.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and pass",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the desired thread name to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Builder::name",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/thread/builder/struct.Builder.html#method.name"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". To retrieve the thread name from within the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "thread, use ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Thread::name",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/thread/thread/struct.Thread.html#method.name"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". A couple of examples where the name of a thread gets used:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "If a panic occurs in a named thread, the thread name will be printed in the panic message.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "The thread name is provided to the OS where applicable (e.g., ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "pthread_setname_np",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " in",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "unix-like platforms).",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Stack size",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The default stack size is platform-dependent and subject to change.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Currently, it is 2 MiB on all Tier-1 platforms.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "There are two ways to manually specify the stack size for spawned threads:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "Build the thread with ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Builder",
                            "style": "InlineCode",
                            "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/thread/builder/struct.Builder.html"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " and pass the desired stack size to ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Builder::stack_size",
                            "style": "InlineCode",
                            "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/thread/builder/struct.Builder.html#method.stack_size"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ".",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "Set the ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "RUST_MIN_STACK",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " environment variable to an integer representing the desired stack",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "size (in bytes). Note that setting ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Builder::stack_size",
                            "style": "InlineCode",
                            "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/thread/builder/struct.Builder.html#method.stack_size"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " will override this. Be aware that",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "changes to ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "RUST_MIN_STACK",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " may be ignored after program start.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Note that the stack size of the main thread is ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "not",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " determined by Rust.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "ascii",
        "kind": "module",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/ascii/index.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Operations on ASCII strings and characters.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Most string operations in Rust act on UTF-8 strings. However, at times it",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "makes more sense to only consider the ASCII character set for a specific",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "operation.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "AsciiExt",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/ascii/trait.AsciiExt.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " trait provides methods that allow for character",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "operations that only act on the ASCII subset and leave non-ASCII characters",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "alone.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "escape_default",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ascii/index.html?search=core%3A%3Aascii%3A%3Aescape%5Fdefault"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " function provides an iterator over the bytes of an",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "escaped version of the character given.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "backtrace",
        "kind": "module",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/backtrace/index.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Support for capturing a stack backtrace of an OS thread",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This module contains the support necessary to capture a stack backtrace of a",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "running OS thread from the OS thread itself. The ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Backtrace",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " type supports",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "capturing a stack trace via the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Backtrace::capture",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Backtrace::force_capture",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " functions.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "A backtrace is typically quite handy to attach to errors (e.g. types",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "implementing ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "std::error::Error",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ") to get a causal chain of where an error",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "was generated.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Accuracy",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Backtraces are attempted to be as accurate as possible, but no guarantees",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "are provided about the exact accuracy of a backtrace. Instruction pointers,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "symbol names, filenames, line numbers, etc, may all be incorrect when",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "reported. Accuracy is attempted on a best-effort basis, however, any bug",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "reports are always welcome to indicate areas of improvement!",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "For most platforms a backtrace with a filename/line number requires that",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "programs be compiled with debug information. Without debug information",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "filenames/line numbers will not be reported.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Platform support",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Not all platforms that std compiles for support capturing backtraces. Some",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "platforms simply do nothing when capturing a backtrace. To check whether the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "platform supports capturing backtraces you can consult the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "BacktraceStatus",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "enum as a result of ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Backtrace::status",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Like above with accuracy platform support is done on a best effort basis.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Sometimes libraries might not be available at runtime or something may go",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "wrong which would cause a backtrace to not be captured. Please feel free to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "report issues with platforms where a backtrace cannot be captured though!",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Environment Variables",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Backtrace::capture",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " function might not actually capture a backtrace by",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "default. Its behavior is governed by two environment variables:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "RUST_LIB_BACKTRACE",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " - if this is set to ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "0",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " then ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Backtrace::capture",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "will never capture a backtrace. Any other value set will enable",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Backtrace::capture",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ".",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "RUST_BACKTRACE",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " - if ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "RUST_LIB_BACKTRACE",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " is not set, then this variable",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "is consulted with the same rules of ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "RUST_LIB_BACKTRACE",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ".",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "If neither of the above env vars are set, then ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Backtrace::capture",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " will",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "be disabled.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Capturing a backtrace can be a quite expensive runtime operation, so the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "environment variables allow either forcibly disabling this runtime",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "performance hit or allow selectively enabling it in some programs.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Note that the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Backtrace::force_capture",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " function can be used to ignore",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "these environment variables. Also note that the state of environment",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "variables is cached once the first backtrace is created, so altering",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "RUST_LIB_BACKTRACE",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " or ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "RUST_BACKTRACE",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " at runtime might not actually change",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "how backtraces are captured.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "bstr",
        "kind": "module",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/bstr/index.html",
        "docs": [
          {
