              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Note that where ties occur, ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vec",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/index.html?search=alloc%3A%3Avec%3A%3AVec"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is generally going to be faster than",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "VecDeque",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/collections/vec_deque/index.html?search=alloc%3A%3Acollections%3A%3Avec%5Fdeque%3A%3AVecDeque"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "VecDeque",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/collections/vec_deque/index.html?search=alloc%3A%3Acollections%3A%3Avec%5Fdeque%3A%3AVecDeque"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is generally going to be faster than",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "LinkedList",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/collections/linked_list/index.html?search=alloc%3A%3Acollections%3A%3Alinked%5Flist%3A%3ALinkedList"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "For Sets, all operations have the cost of the equivalent Map operation.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Correct and Efficient Usage of Collections",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Of course, knowing which collection is the right one for the job doesn't",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "instantly permit you to use it correctly. Here are some quick tips for",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "efficient and correct usage of the standard collections in general. If",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "you're interested in how to use a specific collection in particular, consult",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "its documentation for detailed discussion and code examples.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Capacity Management",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Many collections provide several constructors and methods that refer to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "\"capacity\". These collections are generally built on top of an array.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Optimally, this array would be exactly the right size to fit only the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "elements stored in the collection, but for the collection to do this would",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "be very inefficient. If the backing array was exactly the right size at all",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "times, then every time an element is inserted, the collection would have to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "grow the array to fit it. Due to the way memory is allocated and managed on",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "most computers, this would almost surely require allocating an entirely new",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "array and copying every single element from the old one into the new one.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Hopefully you can see that this wouldn't be very efficient to do on every",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "operation.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Most collections therefore use an ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "amortized",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " allocation strategy. They",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "generally let themselves have a fair amount of unoccupied space so that they",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "only have to grow on occasion. When they do grow, they allocate a",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "substantially larger array to move the elements into so that it will take a",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "while for another grow to be required. While this strategy is great in",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "general, it would be even better if the collection ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "never",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " had to resize its",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "backing array. Unfortunately, the collection itself doesn't have enough",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "information to do this itself. Therefore, it is up to us programmers to give",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "it hints.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Any ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "with_capacity",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " constructor will instruct the collection to allocate",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "enough space for the specified number of elements. Ideally this will be for",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "exactly that many elements, but some implementation details may prevent",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "this. See collection-specific documentation for details. In general, use",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "with_capacity",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " when you know exactly how many elements will be inserted, or",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "at least have a reasonable upper-bound on that number.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "When anticipating a large influx of elements, the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "reserve",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " family of",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "methods can be used to hint to the collection how much room it should make",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "for the coming items. As with ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "with_capacity",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", the precise behavior of",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "these methods will be specific to the collection of interest.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "For optimal performance, collections will generally avoid shrinking",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "themselves. If you believe that a collection will not soon contain any more",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "elements, or just really need the memory, the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "shrink_to_fit",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " method prompts",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the collection to shrink the backing array to the minimum size capable of",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "holding its elements.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Finally, if ever you're interested in what the actual capacity of the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "collection is, most collections provide a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "capacity",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " method to query this",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "information on demand. This can be useful for debugging purposes, or for",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "use with the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "reserve",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " methods.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Iterators",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Iterators",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3Aiter"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "are a powerful and robust mechanism used throughout Rust's",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "standard libraries. Iterators provide a sequence of values in a generic,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "safe, efficient and convenient way. The contents of an iterator are usually",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "lazily",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " evaluated, so that only the values that are actually needed are",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "ever actually produced, and no allocation need be done to temporarily store",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "them. Iterators are primarily consumed using a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "for",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " loop, although many",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "functions also take iterators where a collection or sequence of values is",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "desired.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "All of the standard collections provide several iterators for performing",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "bulk manipulation of their contents. The three primary iterators almost",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "every collection should provide are ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "iter",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "iter_mut",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "into_iter",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Some of these are not provided on collections where it would be unsound or",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "unreasonable to provide them.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "iter",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " provides an iterator of immutable references to all the contents of a",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "collection in the most \"natural\" order. For sequence collections like ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vec",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/index.html?search=alloc%3A%3Avec%3A%3AVec"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ",",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "this means the items will be yielded in increasing order of index starting",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "at 0. For ordered collections like ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "BTreeMap",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/collections/btree/map/index.html?search=alloc%3A%3Acollections%3A%3Abtree%3A%3Amap%3A%3ABTreeMap"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", this means that the items",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "will be yielded in sorted order. For unordered collections like ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "HashMap",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/collections/hash/map/struct.HashMap.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ",",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the items will be yielded in whatever order the internal representation made",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "most convenient. This is great for reading through all the contents of the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "collection.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let vec = vec![1, 2, 3, 4];\nfor x in vec.iter() {\n   println!(\"vec contained {x:?}\");\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "iter_mut",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " provides an iterator of ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "mutable",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " references in the same order as",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "iter",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". This is great for mutating all the contents of the collection.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let mut vec = vec![1, 2, 3, 4];\nfor x in vec.iter_mut() {\n   *x += 1;\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "into_iter",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " transforms the actual collection into an iterator over its",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "contents by-value. This is great when the collection itself is no longer",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "needed, and the values are needed elsewhere. Using ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "extend",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " with ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "into_iter",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "is the main way that contents of one collection are moved into another.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "extend",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " automatically calls ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "into_iter",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", and takes any ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "T: ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "IntoIterator",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/iter/traits/collect/index.html?search=core%3A%3Aiter%3A%3Atraits%3A%3Acollect%3A%3AIntoIterator"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Calling ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "collect",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " on an iterator itself is also a great way to convert one",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "collection into another. Both of these methods should internally use the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "capacity management tools discussed in the previous section to do this as",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "efficiently as possible.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let mut vec1 = vec![1, 2, 3, 4];\nlet vec2 = vec![10, 20, 30, 40];\nvec1.extend(vec2);"
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "use std::collections::VecDeque;\n\nlet vec = [1, 2, 3, 4];\nlet buf: VecDeque<_> = vec.into_iter().collect();"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Iterators also provide a series of ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "adapter",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " methods for performing common",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "threads to sequences. Among the adapters are functional favorites like ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "map",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ",",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "fold",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "skip",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "take",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". Of particular interest to collections is the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "rev",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " adapter, which reverses any iterator that supports this operation. Most",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "collections provide reversible iterators as the way to iterate over them in",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "reverse order.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let vec = vec![1, 2, 3, 4];\nfor x in vec.iter().rev() {\n   println!(\"vec contained {x:?}\");\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Several other collection methods also return iterators to yield a sequence",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "of results but avoid allocating an entire collection to store the result in.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "This provides maximum flexibility as",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "collect",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/iter/Iterator/index.html?search=std%3A%3Aiter%3A%3AIterator%3A%3Acollect"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " or",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "extend",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/iter/Extend/index.html?search=std%3A%3Aiter%3A%3AExtend%3A%3Aextend"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " can be called to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "\"pipe\" the sequence into any collection if desired. Otherwise, the sequence",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "can be looped over with a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "for",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " loop. The iterator can also be discarded",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "after partial use, preventing the computation of the unused items.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Entries",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "entry",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " API is intended to provide an efficient mechanism for",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "manipulating the contents of a map conditionally on the presence of a key or",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "not. The primary motivating use case for this is to provide efficient",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "accumulator maps. For instance, if one wishes to maintain a count of the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "number of times each key has been seen, they will have to perform some",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "conditional logic on whether this is the first time the key has been seen or",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "not. Normally, this would require a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "find",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " followed by an ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "insert",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ",",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "effectively duplicating the search effort on each insertion.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "When a user calls ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "map.entry(key)",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", the map will search for the key and",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "then yield a variant of the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Entry",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " enum.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "If a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vacant(entry)",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is yielded, then the key ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "was not",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " found. In this case",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the only valid operation is to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "insert",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " a value into the entry. When this is",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "done, the vacant entry is consumed and converted into a mutable reference to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the value that was inserted. This allows for further manipulation of the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "value beyond the lifetime of the search itself. This is useful if complex",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "logic needs to be performed on the value regardless of whether the value was",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "just inserted.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "If an ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Occupied(entry)",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is yielded, then the key ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "was",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " found. In this case,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the user has several options: they can ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "get",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "insert",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " or ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "remove",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "value of the occupied entry. Additionally, they can convert the occupied",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "entry into a mutable reference to its value, providing symmetry to the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "vacant ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "insert",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " case.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Here are the two primary ways in which ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "entry",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is used. First, a simple",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "example where the logic performed on the values is trivial.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Counting the number of times each character in a string occurs",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "use std::collections::btree_map::BTreeMap;\n\nlet mut count = BTreeMap::new();\nlet message = \"she sells sea shells by the sea shore\";\n\nfor c in message.chars() {\n    *count.entry(c).or_insert(0) += 1;\n}\n\nassert_eq!(count.get(&'s'), Some(&8));\n\nprintln!(\"Number of occurrences of each character\");\nfor (char, count) in &count {\n    println!(\"{char}: {count}\");\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "When the logic to be performed on the value is more complex, we may simply",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "use the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "entry",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " API to ensure that the value is initialized and perform the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "logic afterwards.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Tracking the inebriation of customers at a bar",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "use std::collections::btree_map::BTreeMap;\n\n// A client of the bar. They have a blood alcohol level.\nstruct Person { blood_alcohol: f32 }\n\n// All the orders made to the bar, by client ID.\nlet orders = vec![1, 2, 1, 2, 3, 4, 1, 2, 2, 3, 4, 1, 1, 1];\n\n// Our clients.\nlet mut blood_alcohol = BTreeMap::new();\n\nfor id in orders {\n    // If this is the first time we've seen this customer, initialize them\n    // with no blood alcohol. Otherwise, just retrieve them.\n    let person = blood_alcohol.entry(id).or_insert(Person { blood_alcohol: 0.0 });\n\n    // Reduce their blood alcohol level. It takes time to order and drink a beer!\n    person.blood_alcohol *= 0.9;\n\n    // Check if they're sober enough to have another beer.\n    if person.blood_alcohol > 0.3 {\n        // Too drunk... for now.\n        println!(\"Sorry {id}, I have to cut you off\");\n    } else {\n        // Have another!\n        person.blood_alcohol += 0.1;\n    }\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Insert and complex keys",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "If we have a more complex key, calls to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "insert",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " will",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "not update the value of the key. For example:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "use std::cmp::Ordering;\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\nuse std::hash::{Hash, Hasher};\n\n#[derive(Debug)]\nstruct Foo {\n    a: u32,\n    b: &'static str,\n}\n\n// we will compare `Foo`s by their `a` value only.\nimpl PartialEq for Foo {\n    fn eq(&self, other: &Self) -> bool { self.a == other.a }\n}\n\nimpl Eq for Foo {}\n\n// we will hash `Foo`s by their `a` value only.\nimpl Hash for Foo {\n    fn hash<H: Hasher>(&self, h: &mut H) { self.a.hash(h); }\n}\n\nimpl PartialOrd for Foo {\n    fn partial_cmp(&self, other: &Self) -> Option<Ordering> { self.a.partial_cmp(&other.a) }\n}\n\nimpl Ord for Foo {\n    fn cmp(&self, other: &Self) -> Ordering { self.a.cmp(&other.a) }\n}\n\nlet mut map = BTreeMap::new();\nmap.insert(Foo { a: 1, b: \"baz\" }, 99);\n\n// We already have a Foo with an a of 1, so this will be updating the value.\nmap.insert(Foo { a: 1, b: \"xyz\" }, 100);\n\n// The value has been updated...\nassert_eq!(map.values().next().unwrap(), &100);\n\n// ...but the key hasn't changed. b is still \"baz\", not \"xyz\".\nassert_eq!(map.keys().next().unwrap().b, \"baz\");"
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
