            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "async_iter",
        "kind": "module",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/async_iter/index.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Composable asynchronous iteration.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "If you've found yourself with an asynchronous collection of some kind,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "and needed to perform an operation on the elements of said collection,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "you'll quickly run into 'async iterators'. Async Iterators are heavily used in",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "idiomatic asynchronous Rust code, so it's worth becoming familiar with them.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Before explaining more, let's talk about how this module is structured:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Organization",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This module is largely organized by type:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "Traits",
                            "style": "Plain",
                            "url": "#traits"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " are the core portion: these traits define what kind of async iterators",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "exist and what you can do with them. The methods of these traits are worth",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "putting some extra study time into.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "Functions provide some helpful ways to create some basic async iterators.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "Structs are often the return types of the various methods on this",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "module's traits. You'll usually want to look at the method that creates",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "the ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "struct",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ", rather than the ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "struct",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " itself. For more detail about why,",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "see '",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Implementing Async Iterator",
                            "style": "Plain",
                            "url": "#implementing-async-iterator"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "'.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "That's it! Let's dig into async iterators.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Async Iterators",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The heart and soul of this module is the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "AsyncIterator",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/async_iter/async_iter/trait.AsyncIterator.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " trait. The core of",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "AsyncIterator",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/async_iter/async_iter/trait.AsyncIterator.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " looks like this:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "trait AsyncIterator {\n    type Item;\n    fn poll_next(self: Pin<&mut Self>, cx: &mut Context<'_>) -> Poll<Option<Self::Item>>;\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Unlike ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Iterator",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "AsyncIterator",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " makes a distinction between the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "poll_next",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "method which is used when implementing an ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "AsyncIterator",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", and a (to-be-implemented)",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "next",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " method which is used when consuming an async iterator. Consumers of ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "AsyncIterator",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "only need to consider ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "next",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", which when called, returns a future which",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "yields ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Option<AsyncIterator::Item>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The future returned by ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "next",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " will yield ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Some(Item)",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " as long as there are",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "elements, and once they've all been exhausted, will yield ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "None",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " to indicate",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "that iteration is finished. If we're waiting on something asynchronous to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "resolve, the future will wait until the async iterator is ready to yield again.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Individual async iterators may choose to resume iteration, and so calling ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "next",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "again may or may not eventually yield ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Some(Item)",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " again at some point.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "AsyncIterator",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/async_iter/async_iter/trait.AsyncIterator.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "'s full definition includes a number of other methods as well,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "but they are default methods, built on top of ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "poll_next",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", and so you get",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "them for free.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Implementing Async Iterator",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Creating an async iterator of your own involves two steps: creating a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "struct",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "hold the async iterator's state, and then implementing ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "AsyncIterator",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/async_iter/async_iter/trait.AsyncIterator.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " for that",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "struct",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Let's make an async iterator named ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Counter",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " which counts from ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "1",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "5",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ":",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "#![feature(async_iterator)]\n\n// First, the struct:\n\n/// An async iterator which counts from one to five\nstruct Counter {\n    count: usize,\n}\n\n// we want our count to start at one, so let's add a new() method to help.\n// This isn't strictly necessary, but is convenient. Note that we start\n// `count` at zero, we'll see why in `poll_next()`'s implementation below.\nimpl Counter {\n    fn new() -> Counter {\n        Counter { count: 0 }\n    }\n}\n\n// Then, we implement `AsyncIterator` for our `Counter`:\n\nimpl AsyncIterator for Counter {\n    // we will be counting with usize\n    type Item = usize;\n\n    // poll_next() is the only required method\n    fn poll_next(mut self: Pin<&mut Self>, cx: &mut Context<'_>) -> Poll<Option<Self::Item>> {\n        // Increment our count. This is why we started at zero.\n        self.count += 1;\n\n        // Check to see if we've finished counting or not.\n        if self.count < 6 {\n            Poll::Ready(Some(self.count))\n        } else {\n            Poll::Ready(None)\n        }\n    }\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Laziness",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Async iterators are ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "lazy",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". This means that just creating an async iterator doesn't",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "do",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " a whole lot. Nothing really happens until you call ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "poll_next",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". This is",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "sometimes a source of confusion when creating an async iterator solely for its side",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "effects. The compiler will warn us about this kind of behavior:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "text",
                "code": "warning: unused result that must be used: async iterators do nothing unless polled\n"
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "cell",
        "kind": "module",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cell/index.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Shareable mutable containers.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Rust memory safety is based on this rule: Given an object ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", it is only possible to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "have one of the following:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "Several immutable references (",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "&T",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ") to the object (also known as ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "aliasing",
                            "style": "Strong"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ").",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "One mutable reference (",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "&mut T",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ") to the object (also known as ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "mutability",
                            "style": "Strong"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ").",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This is enforced by the Rust compiler. However, there are situations where this rule is not",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "flexible enough. Sometimes it is required to have multiple references to an object and yet",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "mutate it.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Shareable mutable containers exist to permit mutability in a controlled manner, even in the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "presence of aliasing. ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cell<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cell/struct.Cell.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "RefCell<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cell/struct.RefCell.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "OnceCell<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cell/once/struct.OnceCell.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " allow doing this in",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "a single-threaded way—they do not implement ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Sync",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fstd%2Fmarker%2Ftrait%2ESync"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". (If you need to do aliasing and",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "mutation among multiple threads, ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Mutex<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fstd%2Fsync%2Fstruct%2EMutex"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "RwLock<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fstd%2Fsync%2Fstruct%2ERwLock"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "OnceLock<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fstd%2Fsync%2Fstruct%2EOnceLock"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " or ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "atomic",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/sync/atomic/index.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "types are the correct data structures to do so).",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Values of the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cell<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "RefCell<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "OnceCell<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " types may be mutated through shared",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "references (i.e. the common ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " type), whereas most Rust types can only be mutated through",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "unique (",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&mut T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ") references. We say these cell types provide 'interior mutability'",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "(mutable via ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "), in contrast with typical Rust types that exhibit 'inherited mutability'",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "(mutable only via ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&mut T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ").",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Cell types come in four flavors: ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cell<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "RefCell<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "OnceCell<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "LazyCell<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Each provides a different way of providing safe interior mutability.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Cell<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Cell<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cell/struct.Cell.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " implements interior mutability by moving values in and out of the cell. That is, a",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " to the inner value can never be obtained, and the value itself cannot be directly",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "obtained without replacing it with something else. This type provides the following",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "methods:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "For types that implement ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Copy",
                            "style": "InlineCode",
                            "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/marker/trait.Copy.html"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ", the ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "get",
