              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Cell<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is typically used for more simple types where copying or moving values isn't too",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "resource intensive (e.g. numbers), and should usually be preferred over other cell types when",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "possible. For larger and non-copy types, ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "RefCell",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " provides some advantages.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "RefCell<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "RefCell<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cell/struct.RefCell.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " uses Rust's lifetimes to implement \"dynamic borrowing\", a process whereby one can",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "claim temporary, exclusive, mutable access to the inner value. Borrows for ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "RefCell<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "s are",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "tracked at ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "runtime",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", unlike Rust's native reference types which are entirely tracked",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "statically, at compile time.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "An immutable reference to a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "RefCell",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "'s inner value (",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ") can be obtained with",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "borrow",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cell/struct.RefCell.html#method.borrow"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", and a mutable borrow (",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&mut T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ") can be obtained with",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "borrow_mut",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cell/struct.RefCell.html#method.borrow_mut"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". When these functions are called, they first verify that",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Rust's borrow rules will be satisfied: any number of immutable borrows are allowed or a",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "single mutable borrow is allowed, but never both. If a borrow is attempted that would violate",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "these rules, the thread will panic.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The corresponding ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Sync",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fstd%2Fmarker%2Ftrait%2ESync"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " version of ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "RefCell<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "RwLock<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fstd%2Fsync%2Fstruct%2ERwLock"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "OnceCell<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  }
