      {
        "path": "clone",
        "kind": "module",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/clone/index.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Clone",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " trait for types that cannot be 'implicitly copied'.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "In Rust, some simple types are \"implicitly copyable\" and when you",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "assign them or pass them as arguments, the receiver will get a copy,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "leaving the original value in place. These types do not require",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "allocation to copy and do not have finalizers (i.e., they do not",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "contain owned boxes or implement ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Drop",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ops/drop/trait.Drop.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "), so the compiler considers",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "them cheap and safe to copy. For other types copies must be made",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "explicitly, by convention implementing the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Clone",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " trait and calling",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "clone",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " method.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Basic usage example:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let s = String::new(); // String type implements Clone\nlet copy = s.clone(); // so we can clone it"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "To easily implement the Clone trait, you can also use",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "#[derive(Clone)]",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". Example:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "#[derive(Clone)] // we add the Clone trait to Morpheus struct\nstruct Morpheus {\n   blue_pill: f32,\n   red_pill: i64,\n}\n\nfn main() {\n   let f = Morpheus { blue_pill: 0.0, red_pill: 0 };\n   let copy = f.clone(); // and now we can clone it!\n}"
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "cmp",
        "kind": "module",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cmp/index.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Utilities for comparing and ordering values.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This module contains various tools for comparing and ordering values. In",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "summary:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "PartialEq<Rhs>",
                            "style": "InlineCode",
                            "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cmp/trait.PartialEq.html"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " overloads the ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "==",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " and ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "!=",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " operators. In cases where",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Rhs",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " (the right hand side's type) is ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Self",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ", this trait corresponds to a",
