      },
      {
        "path": "iter",
        "kind": "module",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/iter/index.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Composable external iteration.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "If you've found yourself with a collection of some kind, and needed to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "perform an operation on the elements of said collection, you'll quickly run",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "into 'iterators'. Iterators are heavily used in idiomatic Rust code, so",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "it's worth becoming familiar with them.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Before explaining more, let's talk about how this module is structured:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Organization",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This module is largely organized by type:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "Traits",
                            "style": "Plain",
                            "url": "#traits"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " are the core portion: these traits define what kind of iterators",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "exist and what you can do with them. The methods of these traits are worth",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "putting some extra study time into.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "Functions",
                            "style": "Plain",
                            "url": "#functions"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " provide some helpful ways to create some basic iterators.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "Structs",
                            "style": "Plain",
                            "url": "#structs"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " are often the return types of the various methods on this",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "module's traits. You'll usually want to look at the method that creates",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "the ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "struct",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ", rather than the ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "struct",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " itself. For more detail about why,",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "see '",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Implementing Iterator",
                            "style": "Plain",
                            "url": "#implementing-iterator"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "'.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "That's it! Let's dig into iterators.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Iterator",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The heart and soul of this module is the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Iterator",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/iter/traits/iterator/trait.Iterator.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " trait. The core of",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Iterator",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/iter/traits/iterator/trait.Iterator.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " looks like this:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "trait Iterator {\n    type Item;\n    fn next(&mut self) -> Option<Self::Item>;\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "An iterator has a method, ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "next",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", which when called, returns an",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Option",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/option/enum.Option.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "<Item>",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". Calling ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "next",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " will return ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Some(Item)",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " as long as there",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "are elements, and once they've all been exhausted, will return ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "None",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "indicate that iteration is finished. Individual iterators may choose to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "resume iteration, and so calling ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "next",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " again may or may not eventually",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "start returning ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Some(Item)",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " again at some point (for example, see ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "TryIter",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fstd%2Fsync%2Fmpsc%2Fstruct%2ETryIter"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ").",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Iterator",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/iter/traits/iterator/trait.Iterator.html"
                  },
