              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let values = vec![1, 2, 3, 4, 5];\n\nfor x in values {\n    println!(\"{x}\");\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This will print the numbers one through five, each on their own line. But",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "you'll notice something here: we never called anything on our vector to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "produce an iterator. What gives?",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "There's a trait in the standard library for converting something into an",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
