      {
        "path": "ops",
        "kind": "module",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ops/index.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Overloadable operators.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Implementing these traits allows you to overload certain operators.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Some of these traits are imported by the prelude, so they are available in",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "every Rust program. Only operators backed by traits can be overloaded. For",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "example, the addition operator (",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "+",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ") can be overloaded through the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Add",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ops/arith/trait.Add.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "trait, but since the assignment operator (",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "=",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ") has no backing trait, there",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "is no way of overloading its semantics. Additionally, this module does not",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "provide any mechanism to create new operators. If traitless overloading or",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "custom operators are required, you should look toward macros to extend",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Rust's syntax.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Implementations of operator traits should be unsurprising in their",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "respective contexts, keeping in mind their usual meanings and",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "operator precedence",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Freference%2Fexpressions"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". For example, when implementing ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Mul",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ops/arith/trait.Mul.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", the operation",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "should have some resemblance to multiplication (and share expected",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "properties like associativity).",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Note that the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&&",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "||",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " operators are currently not supported for",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "overloading. Due to their short circuiting nature, they require a different",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "design from traits for other operators like ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "BitAnd",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ops/bit/trait.BitAnd.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". Designs for them are",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "under discussion.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Many of the operators take their operands by value. In non-generic",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "contexts involving built-in types, this is usually not a problem.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "However, using these operators in generic code, requires some",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "attention if values have to be reused as opposed to letting the operators",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "consume them. One option is to occasionally use ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "clone",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Another option is to rely on the types involved providing additional",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "operator implementations for references. For example, for a user-defined",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "type ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " which is supposed to support addition, it is probably a good",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "idea to have both ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " implement the traits ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Add<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ops/arith/trait.Add.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Add<&T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ops/arith/trait.Add.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " so that generic code can be written without unnecessary",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "cloning.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This example creates a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Point",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " struct that implements ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Add",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ops/arith/trait.Add.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Sub",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ops/arith/trait.Sub.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ",",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "and then demonstrates adding and subtracting two ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Point",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "s.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "use std::ops::{Add, Sub};\n\n#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq)]\nstruct Point {\n    x: i32,\n    y: i32,\n}\n\nimpl Add for Point {\n    type Output = Self;\n\n    fn add(self, other: Self) -> Self {\n        Self {x: self.x + other.x, y: self.y + other.y}\n    }\n}\n\nimpl Sub for Point {\n    type Output = Self;\n\n    fn sub(self, other: Self) -> Self {\n        Self {x: self.x - other.x, y: self.y - other.y}\n    }\n}\n\nassert_eq!(Point {x: 3, y: 3}, Point {x: 1, y: 0} + Point {x: 2, y: 3});\nassert_eq!(Point {x: -1, y: -3}, Point {x: 1, y: 0} - Point {x: 2, y: 3});"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "See the documentation for each trait for an example implementation.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Fn",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ops/function/trait.Fn.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "FnMut",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ops/function/trait.FnMut.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "FnOnce",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ops/function/trait.FnOnce.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " traits are implemented by types that can be",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "invoked like functions. Note that ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Fn",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ops/function/trait.Fn.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " takes ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&self",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "FnMut",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ops/function/trait.FnMut.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " takes ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&mut self",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "FnOnce",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ops/function/trait.FnOnce.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " takes ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "self",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". These correspond to the three kinds of",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "methods that can be invoked on an instance: call-by-reference,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "call-by-mutable-reference, and call-by-value. The most common use of these",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "traits is to act as bounds to higher-level functions that take functions or",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "closures as arguments.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Taking a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Fn",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ops/function/trait.Fn.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " as a parameter:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "fn call_with_one<F>(func: F) -> usize\n    where F: Fn(usize) -> usize\n{\n    func(1)\n}\n\nlet double = |x| x * 2;\nassert_eq!(call_with_one(double), 2);"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Taking a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "FnMut",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ops/function/trait.FnMut.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " as a parameter:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "fn do_twice<F>(mut func: F)\n    where F: FnMut()\n{\n    func();\n    func();\n}\n\nlet mut x: usize = 1;\n{\n    let add_two_to_x = || x += 2;\n    do_twice(add_two_to_x);\n}\n\nassert_eq!(x, 5);"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Taking a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "FnOnce",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ops/function/trait.FnOnce.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " as a parameter:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "fn consume_with_relish<F>(func: F)\n    where F: FnOnce() -> String\n{\n    // `func` consumes its captured variables, so it cannot be run more\n    // than once\n    println!(\"Consumed: {}\", func());\n\n    println!(\"Delicious!\");\n\n    // Attempting to invoke `func()` again will throw a `use of moved\n    // value` error for `func`\n}\n\nlet x = String::from(\"x\");\nlet consume_and_return_x = move || x;\nconsume_with_relish(consume_and_return_x);\n\n// `consume_and_return_x` can no longer be invoked at this point"
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "option",
        "kind": "module",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/option/index.html",
        "docs": [
