      {
        "path": "ptr",
        "kind": "module",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ptr/index.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Manually manage memory through raw pointers.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "See also the pointer primitive types",
                    "style": "Emphasis",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/primitive.pointer.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Safety",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Many functions in this module take raw pointers as arguments and read from or write to them. For",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "this to be safe, these pointers must be ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "valid",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " for the given access. Whether a pointer is valid",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "depends on the operation it is used for (read or write), and the extent of the memory that is",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "accessed (i.e., how many bytes are read/written) -- it makes no sense to ask \"is this pointer",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "valid\"; one has to ask \"is this pointer valid for a given access\". Most functions use ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "*mut T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "*const T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " to access only a single value, in which case the documentation omits the size and",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "implicitly assumes it to be ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "size_of::<T>()",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " bytes.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The precise rules for validity are not determined yet. The guarantees that are",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "provided at this point are very minimal:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "A ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "null",
                            "style": "Plain",
                            "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ptr/fn.null.html"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " pointer is ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "never",
                            "style": "Emphasis"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " valid for reads/writes.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "For memory accesses of ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "size zero",
                            "style": "Plain",
                            "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fnomicon%2Fexotic%2Dsizes"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ", ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "every",
                            "style": "Emphasis"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " non-null pointer is valid for reads/writes.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "The following points are only concerned with non-zero-sized accesses.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "For a pointer to be valid for reads/writes, it is necessary, but not always sufficient, that",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "the pointer be ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "dereferenceable",
                            "style": "Emphasis"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ". The ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "provenance",
                            "style": "Plain",
                            "url": "#provenance"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " of the pointer is used to determine which",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "allocation",
                            "style": "Plain",
                            "url": "#allocation"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " it is derived from; a pointer is dereferenceable if the memory range of the given",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "size starting at the pointer is entirely contained within the bounds of that allocation. Note",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "that in Rust, every (stack-allocated) variable is considered a separate allocation.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "All accesses performed by functions in this module are ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "non-atomic",
                            "style": "Emphasis"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " in the sense",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "of ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "atomic operations",
                            "style": "Plain",
                            "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/sync/atomic/index.html"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " used to synchronize between threads. This means it is",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "undefined behavior to perform two concurrent accesses to the same location from different",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "threads unless both accesses only read from memory.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "The result of casting a reference to a pointer is valid for reads/writes for as long as the",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "underlying allocation is live and no reference (just raw pointers) is used to",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "access the same memory. That is, reference and pointer accesses cannot be",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "interleaved.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "These axioms, along with careful use of ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "offset",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " for pointer arithmetic,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "are enough to correctly implement many useful things in unsafe code. Stronger guarantees",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "will be provided eventually, as the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "aliasing",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fnomicon%2Faliasing"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " rules are being determined. For more",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "information, see the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "book",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fbook%2Fch19%2D01%2Dunsafe%2Drust"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " as well as the section in the reference devoted",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "undefined behavior",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Freference%2Fbehavior%2Dconsidered%2Dundefined"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Note that some operations such as ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "read",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ptr/fn.read.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "write",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ptr/fn.write.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " do allow null pointers if",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the total size of the access is zero. However, other operations internally convert pointers into",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "references. Therefore, the general notion of \"valid for reads/writes\" excludes null pointers,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "and the specific operations that permit null pointers mention that as an exception. Furthermore,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "read_volatile",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ptr/fn.read_volatile.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "write_volatile",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ptr/fn.write_volatile.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " can be used in even more situations; see their",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "documentation for details.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "We say that a pointer is \"dangling\" if it is not valid for any non-zero-sized accesses. This",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "means out-of-bounds pointers, pointers to freed memory, null pointers, and pointers created with",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "NonNull::dangling",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ptr/non_null/struct.NonNull.html#method.dangling"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " are all dangling.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Alignment",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Valid raw pointers as defined above are not necessarily properly aligned (where",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "\"proper\" alignment is defined by the pointee type, i.e., ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "*const T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " must be",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "aligned to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "align_of::<T>()",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "). However, most functions require their",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "arguments to be properly aligned, and will explicitly state",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "this requirement in their documentation. Notable exceptions to this are",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "read_unaligned",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ptr/fn.read_unaligned.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "write_unaligned",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ptr/fn.write_unaligned.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "When a function requires proper alignment, it does so even if the access",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "has size 0, i.e., even if memory is not actually touched. Consider using",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "NonNull::dangling",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ptr/non_null/struct.NonNull.html#method.dangling"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " in such cases.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Pointer to reference conversion",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "When converting a pointer to a reference (e.g. via ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&*ptr",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " or ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&mut *ptr",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "),",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "there are several rules that must be followed:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "The pointer must be properly aligned.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "It must be non-null.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "It must be \"dereferenceable\" in the sense defined above.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "The pointer must point to a ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "valid value",
                            "style": "Plain",
                            "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Freference%2Fbehavior%2Dconsidered%2Dundefined"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " of type ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "T",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ".",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "You must enforce Rust's aliasing rules. The exact aliasing rules are not decided yet, so we",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "only give a rough overview here. The rules also depend on whether a mutable or a shared",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "reference is being created.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "list",
                        "items": [
                          {
                            "content": [
                              {
                                "type": "paragraph",
                                "spans": [
                                  {
                                    "text": "When creating a mutable reference, then while this reference exists, the memory it points to",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": " ",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": "must not get accessed (read or written) through any other pointer or reference not derived",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": " ",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": "from this reference.",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  }
                                ]
                              }
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "content": [
                              {
                                "type": "paragraph",
                                "spans": [
                                  {
                                    "text": "When creating a shared reference, then while this reference exists, the memory it points to",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": " ",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": "must not get mutated (except inside ",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": "UnsafeCell",
                                    "style": "InlineCode"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": ").",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  }
                                ]
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "If a pointer follows all of these rules, it is said to be",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "convertible to a (mutable or shared) reference",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "These rules apply even if the result is unused!",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "(The part about being initialized is not yet fully decided, but until",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "it is, the only safe approach is to ensure that they are indeed initialized.)",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "An example of the implications of the above rules is that an expression such",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "as ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "unsafe { &*(0 as *const u8) }",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is Immediate Undefined Behavior.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Allocation",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "An ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "allocation",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is a subset of program memory which is addressable",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "from Rust, and within which pointer arithmetic is possible. Examples of",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "allocations include heap allocations, stack-allocated variables,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "statics, and consts. The safety preconditions of some Rust operations -",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "such as ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "offset",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and field projections (",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "expr.field",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ") - are defined in",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "terms of the allocations on which they operate.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "An allocation has a base address, a size, and a set of memory",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "addresses. It is possible for an allocation to have zero size, but",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "such an allocation will still have a base address. The base address",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "of an allocation is not necessarily unique. While it is currently the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "case that an allocation always has a set of memory addresses which is",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "fully contiguous (i.e., has no \"holes\"), there is no guarantee that this",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "will not change in the future.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Allocations must behave like \"normal\" memory: in particular, reads must not have",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "side-effects, and writes must become visible to other threads using the usual synchronization",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "primitives.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "For any allocation with ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "base",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " address, ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "size",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", and a set of",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "addresses",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", the following are guaranteed:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "For all addresses ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "a",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " in ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "addresses",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ", ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "a",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " is in the range ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "base .. (base + size)",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " (note that this requires ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "a < base + size",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ", not ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "a <= base + size",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ")",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "base",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " is not equal to ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "null()",
                            "style": "InlineCode",
                            "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ptr/fn.null.html"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " (i.e., the address with the numerical",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "value 0)",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "base + size <= usize::MAX",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "size <= isize::MAX",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "As a consequence of these guarantees, given any address ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "a",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " within the set",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "of addresses of an allocation:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "It is guaranteed that ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "a - base",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " does not overflow ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "isize",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "It is guaranteed that ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "a - base",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " is non-negative",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "It is guaranteed that, given ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "o = a - base",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " (i.e., the offset of ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "a",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " within",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "the allocation), ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "base + o",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " will not wrap around the address space (in",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "other words, will not overflow ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "usize",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ")",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Provenance",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Pointers are not ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "simply",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " an \"integer\" or \"address\". For instance, it's uncontroversial",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "to say that a Use After Free is clearly Undefined Behavior, even if you \"get lucky\"",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "and the freed memory gets reallocated before your read/write (in fact this is the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "worst-case scenario, UAFs would be much less concerning if this didn't happen!).",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "As another example, consider that ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "wrapping_offset",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is documented to \"remember\"",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the allocation that the original pointer points to, even if it is offset far",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "outside the memory range occupied by that allocation.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "To rationalize claims like this, pointers need to somehow be ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "more",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " than just their addresses:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "they must have ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "provenance",
                    "style": "Strong"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "A pointer value in Rust semantically contains the following information:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "The ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "address",
                            "style": "Strong"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " it points to, which can be represented by a ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "usize",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ".",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "The ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "provenance",
                            "style": "Strong"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " it has, defining the memory it has permission to access. Provenance can be",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "absent, in which case the pointer does not have permission to access any memory.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The exact structure of provenance is not yet specified, but the permission defined by a",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "pointer's provenance have a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "spatial",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " component, a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "temporal",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " component, and a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "mutability",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "component:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "Spatial: The set of memory addresses that the pointer is allowed to access.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "Temporal: The timespan during which the pointer is allowed to access those memory addresses.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "Mutability: Whether the pointer may only access the memory for reads, or also access it for",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "writes. Note that this can interact with the other components, e.g. a pointer might permit",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "mutation only for a subset of addresses, or only for a subset of its maximal timespan.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "When an ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "allocation",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "#allocation"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is created, it has a unique Original Pointer. For alloc",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "APIs this is literally the pointer the call returns, and for local variables and statics,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "this is the name of the variable/static. (This is mildly overloading the term \"pointer\"",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "for the sake of brevity/exposition.)",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The Original Pointer for an allocation has provenance that constrains the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "spatial",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "permissions of this pointer to the memory range of the allocation, and the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "temporal",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "permissions to the lifetime of the allocation. Provenance is implicitly inherited by all",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "pointers transitively derived from the Original Pointer through operations like ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "offset",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ",",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "borrowing, and pointer casts. Some operations may ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "shrink",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " the permissions of the derived",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "provenance, limiting how much memory it can access or how long it's valid for (i.e. borrowing a",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "subfield and subslicing can shrink the spatial component of provenance, and all borrowing can",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "shrink the temporal component of provenance). However, no operation can ever ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "grow",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "permissions of the derived provenance: even if you \"know\" there is a larger allocation, you",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "can't derive a pointer with a larger provenance. Similarly, you cannot \"recombine\" two",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "contiguous provenances back into one (i.e. with a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "fn merge(&[T], &[T]) -> &[T]",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ").",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "A reference to a place always has provenance over at least the memory that place occupies.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "A reference to a slice always has provenance over at least the range that slice describes.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Whether and when exactly the provenance of a reference gets \"shrunk\" to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "exactly",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " fit",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the memory it points to is not yet determined.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "A ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "shared",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " reference only ever has provenance that permits reading from memory,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "and never permits writes, except inside ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "UnsafeCell",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cell/struct.UnsafeCell.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Provenance can affect whether a program has undefined behavior:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "It is undefined behavior to access memory through a pointer that does not have provenance over",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "that memory. Note that a pointer \"at the end\" of its provenance is not actually outside its",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "provenance, it just has 0 bytes it can load/store. Zero-sized accesses do not require any",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "provenance since they access an empty range of memory.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "It is undefined behavior to ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "offset",
                            "style": "InlineCode",
                            "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " a pointer across a memory range that is not contained",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "in the allocation it is derived from, or to ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "offset_from",
                            "style": "InlineCode",
                            "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " two pointers not derived",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "from the same allocation. Provenance is used to say what exactly \"derived from\" even",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "means: the lineage of a pointer is traced back to the Original Pointer it descends from, and",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "that identifies the relevant allocation. In particular, it's always UB to offset a",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "pointer derived from something that is now deallocated, except if the offset is 0.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "But it ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "is",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " still sound to:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "Create a pointer without provenance from just an address (see ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "without_provenance",
                            "style": "InlineCode",
                            "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ptr/fn.without_provenance.html"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "). Such a",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "pointer cannot be used for memory accesses (except for zero-sized accesses). This can still be",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "useful for sentinel values like ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "null",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "or",
                            "style": "Emphasis"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " to represent a tagged pointer that will never be",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "dereferenceable. In general, it is always sound for an integer to pretend to be a pointer \"for",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "fun\" as long as you don't use operations on it which require it to be valid (non-zero-sized",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "offset, read, write, etc).",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "Forge an allocation of size zero at any sufficiently aligned non-null address.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "i.e. the usual \"ZSTs are fake, do what you want\" rules apply.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "wrapping_offset",
                            "style": "InlineCode",
                            "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " a pointer outside its provenance. This includes pointers",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "which have \"no\" provenance. In particular, this makes it sound to do pointer tagging tricks.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "Compare arbitrary pointers by address. Pointer comparison ignores provenance and addresses",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "are",
                            "style": "Emphasis"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " just integers, so there is always a coherent answer, even if the pointers are dangling",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "or from different provenances. Note that if you get \"lucky\" and notice that a pointer at the",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "end of one allocation is the \"same\" address as the start of another allocation,",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "anything you do with that fact is ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "probably",
                            "style": "Emphasis"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " going to be gibberish. The scope of that",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "gibberish is kept under control by the fact that the two pointers ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "still",
                            "style": "Emphasis"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " aren't allowed to",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "access the other's allocation (bytes), because they still have different provenance.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Note that the full definition of provenance in Rust is not decided yet, as this interacts",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "with the as-yet undecided ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "aliasing",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fnomicon%2Faliasing"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " rules.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Pointers Vs Integers",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "From this discussion, it becomes very clear that a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "usize",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "cannot",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " accurately represent a pointer,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "and converting from a pointer to a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "usize",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is generally an operation which ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "only",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " extracts the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "address. Converting this address back into pointer requires somehow answering the question:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "which provenance should the resulting pointer have?",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Rust provides two ways of dealing with this situation: ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Strict Provenance",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Exposed Provenance",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Note that a pointer ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "can",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " represent a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "usize",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " (via ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "without_provenance",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ptr/fn.without_provenance.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "), so the right type to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "use in situations where a value is \"sometimes a pointer and sometimes a bare ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "usize",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "\" is a",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "pointer type.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Strict Provenance",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "\"Strict Provenance\" refers to a set of APIs designed to make working with provenance more",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "explicit. They are intended as substitutes for casting a pointer to an integer and back.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Entirely avoiding integer-to-pointer casts successfully side-steps the inherent ambiguity of",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "that operation. This benefits compiler optimizations, and it is pretty much a requirement for",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "using tools like ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Miri",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/miri"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and architectures like ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "CHERI",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://www.cl.cam.ac.uk/research/security/ctsrd/cheri/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " that aim to detect and diagnose pointer",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "misuse.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The key insight to making programming without integer-to-pointer casts ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "at all",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " viable is the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "with_addr",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " method:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "text",
                "code": "/// Creates a new pointer with the given address and the provenance  of `self`.\n///\n/// This is similar to a `addr as *const T` cast,\n/// but copies the provenance of `self` to the new pointer.\n/// This avoids the inherent ambiguity of the unary cast.\n///\n/// This is equivalent to using `wrapping_offset` to offset `self` to the given address,\n/// and therefore has all the same capabilities and restrictions.\npub fn with_addr(self, addr: usize) -> Self;\n"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "So you're still able to drop down to the address representation and do whatever",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "clever bit tricks you want ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "as long as",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " you're able to keep around a pointer",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "into the allocation you care about that can \"reconstitute\" the provenance.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Usually this is very easy, because you only are taking a pointer, messing with the address,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "and then immediately converting back to a pointer. To make this use case more ergonomic,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "we provide the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "map_addr",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " method.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "To help make it clear that code is \"following\" Strict Provenance semantics, we also provide an",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "addr",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " method which promises that the returned address is not part of a",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "pointer-integer-pointer roundtrip. In the future we may provide a lint for pointer",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "<",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "->integer",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "casts to help you audit if your code conforms to strict provenance.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Using Strict Provenance",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Most code needs no changes to conform to strict provenance, as the only really concerning",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "operation is casts from ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "usize",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " to a pointer. For code which ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "does",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " cast a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "usize",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " to a pointer,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the scope of the change depends on exactly what you're doing.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "In general, you just need to make sure that if you want to convert a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "usize",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " address to a",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "pointer and then use that pointer to read/write memory, you need to keep around a pointer",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "that has sufficient provenance to perform that read/write itself. In this way all of your",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "casts from an address to a pointer are essentially just applying offsets/indexing.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This is generally trivial to do for simple cases like tagged pointers ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "as long as you",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "represent the tagged pointer as an actual pointer and not a ",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "usize",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". For instance:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "unsafe {\n    // A flag we want to pack into our pointer\n    static HAS_DATA: usize = 0x1;\n    static FLAG_MASK: usize = !HAS_DATA;\n\n    // Our value, which must have enough alignment to have spare least-significant-bits.\n    let my_precious_data: u32 = 17;\n    assert!(align_of::<u32>() > 1);\n\n    // Create a tagged pointer\n    let ptr = &my_precious_data as *const u32;\n    let tagged = ptr.map_addr(|addr| addr | HAS_DATA);\n\n    // Check the flag:\n    if tagged.addr() & HAS_DATA != 0 {\n        // Untag and read the pointer\n        let data = *tagged.map_addr(|addr| addr & FLAG_MASK);\n        assert_eq!(data, 17);\n    } else {\n        unreachable!()\n    }\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "(Yes, if you've been using ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "AtomicUsize",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/sync/atomic/type.AtomicUsize.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " for pointers in concurrent datastructures, you should",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "be using ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "AtomicPtr",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/sync/atomic/type.AtomicPtr.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " instead. If that messes up the way you atomically manipulate pointers,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "we would like to know why, and what needs to be done to fix it.)",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Situations where a valid pointer ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "must",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " be created from just an address, such as baremetal code",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "accessing a memory-mapped interface at a fixed address, cannot currently be handled with strict",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "provenance APIs and should use ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "exposed provenance",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "#exposed-provenance"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Exposed Provenance",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "As discussed above, integer-to-pointer casts are not possible with Strict Provenance APIs.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "This is by design: the goal of Strict Provenance is to provide a clear specification that we are",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "confident can be formalized unambiguously and can be subject to precise formal reasoning.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Integer-to-pointer casts do not (currently) have such a clear specification.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "However, there exist situations where integer-to-pointer casts cannot be avoided, or",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "where avoiding them would require major refactoring. Legacy platform APIs also regularly assume",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "that ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "usize",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " can capture all the information that makes up a pointer.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Bare-metal platforms can also require the synthesis of a pointer \"out of thin air\" without",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "anywhere to obtain proper provenance from.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Rust's model for dealing with integer-to-pointer casts is called ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Exposed Provenance",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". However,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the semantics of Exposed Provenance are on much less solid footing than Strict Provenance, and",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "at this point it is not yet clear whether a satisfying unambiguous semantics can be defined for",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Exposed Provenance. (If that sounds bad, be reassured that other popular languages that provide",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "integer-to-pointer casts are not faring any better.) Furthermore, Exposed Provenance will not",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "work (well) with tools like ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Miri",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/miri"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "CHERI",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://www.cl.cam.ac.uk/research/security/ctsrd/cheri/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Exposed Provenance is provided by the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "expose_provenance",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "with_exposed_provenance",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ptr/fn.with_exposed_provenance.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " methods,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "which are equivalent to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "as",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " casts between pointers and integers.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "expose_provenance",
                            "style": "InlineCode",
                            "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " is a lot like ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "addr",
                            "style": "InlineCode",
                            "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ", but additionally adds the provenance of the",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "pointer to a global list of 'exposed' provenances. (This list is purely conceptual, it exists",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "for the purpose of specifying Rust but is not materialized in actual executions, except in",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "tools like ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Miri",
                            "style": "Plain",
                            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/miri"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ".)",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Memory which is outside the control of the Rust abstract machine (MMIO registers, for example)",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "is always considered to be exposed, so long as this memory is disjoint from memory that will",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "be used by the abstract machine such as the stack, heap, and statics.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "with_exposed_provenance",
                            "style": "InlineCode",
                            "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ptr/fn.with_exposed_provenance.html"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " can be used to construct a pointer with one of these previously",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "'exposed' provenances. ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "with_exposed_provenance",
                            "style": "InlineCode",
                            "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ptr/fn.with_exposed_provenance.html"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " takes only ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "addr: usize",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " as arguments, so",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "unlike in ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "with_addr",
                            "style": "InlineCode",
                            "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " there is no indication of what the correct provenance for the returned",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "pointer is -- and that is exactly what makes integer-to-pointer casts so tricky to rigorously",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "specify! The compiler will do its best to pick the right provenance for you, but currently we",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "cannot provide any guarantees about which provenance the resulting pointer will have. Only one",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "thing is clear: if there is ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "no",
                            "style": "Emphasis"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " previously 'exposed' provenance that justifies the way the",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "returned pointer will be used, the program has undefined behavior.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "If at all possible, we encourage code to be ported to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Strict Provenance",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "#strict-provenance"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " APIs, thus avoiding",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the need for Exposed Provenance. Maximizing the amount of such code is a major win for avoiding",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "specification complexity and to facilitate adoption of tools like ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "CHERI",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://www.cl.cam.ac.uk/research/security/ctsrd/cheri/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Miri",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/miri"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " that can be",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "a big help in increasing the confidence in (unsafe) Rust code. However, we acknowledge that this",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "is not always possible, and offer Exposed Provenance as a way to explicit \"opt out\" of the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "well-defined semantics of Strict Provenance, and \"opt in\" to the unclear semantics of",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "integer-to-pointer casts.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
