      {
        "path": "boxed",
        "kind": "module",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/boxed/index.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " type for heap allocation.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Box<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/boxed/struct.Box.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", casually referred to as a 'box', provides the simplest form of",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "heap allocation in Rust. Boxes provide ownership for this allocation, and",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "drop their contents when they go out of scope. Boxes also ensure that they",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "never allocate more than ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "isize::MAX",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " bytes.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Move a value from the stack to the heap by creating a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/boxed/struct.Box.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ":",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let val: u8 = 5;\nlet boxed: Box<u8> = Box::new(val);"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Move a value from a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/boxed/struct.Box.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " back to the stack by ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "dereferencing",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ops/deref/index.html?search=core%3A%3Aops%3A%3Aderef%3A%3ADeref"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ":",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let boxed: Box<u8> = Box::new(5);\nlet val: u8 = *boxed;"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Creating a recursive data structure:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "#[derive(Debug)]\nenum List<T> {\n    Cons(T, Box<List<T>>),\n    Nil,\n}\n\nlet list: List<i32> = List::Cons(1, Box::new(List::Cons(2, Box::new(List::Nil))));\nprintln!(\"{list:?}\");"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This will print ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cons(1, Cons(2, Nil))",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Recursive structures must be boxed, because if the definition of ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cons",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "looked like this:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "Cons(T, List<T>),"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "It wouldn't work. This is because the size of a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "List",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " depends on how many",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "elements are in the list, and so we don't know how much memory to allocate",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "for a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cons",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". By introducing a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/boxed/struct.Box.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", which has a defined size, we know how",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "big ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cons",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " needs to be.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Memory layout",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "For non-zero-sized values, a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/boxed/struct.Box.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " will use the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Global",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/alloc/struct.Global.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " allocator for its allocation. It is",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "valid to convert both ways between a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/boxed/struct.Box.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and a raw pointer allocated with the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Global",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/alloc/struct.Global.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "allocator, given that the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Layout",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/alloc/layout/index.html?search=core%3A%3Aalloc%3A%3Alayout%3A%3ALayout"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " used with the allocator is correct for the type and the raw",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "pointer points to a valid value of the right type. More precisely, a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "value: *mut T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " that has",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "been allocated with the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Global",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/alloc/struct.Global.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " allocator with ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Layout::for_value(&*value)",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " may be converted",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "into a box using ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box::<T>::from_raw(value)",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/boxed/struct.Box.html#method.from_raw"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". Conversely, the memory backing a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "value: *mut T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "obtained from ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box::<T>::into_raw",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/boxed/struct.Box.html#method.into_raw"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " may be deallocated using the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Global",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/alloc/struct.Global.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " allocator with",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Layout::for_value(&*value)",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/alloc/Layout/index.html?search=alloc%3A%3Aalloc%3A%3ALayout%3A%3Afor%5Fvalue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "For zero-sized values, the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " pointer has to be non-null and sufficiently aligned. The",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "recommended way to build a Box to a ZST if ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box::new",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " cannot be used is to use",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "ptr::NonNull::dangling",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://docs.rs/ptr/latest/ptr/NonNull/index.html?search=ptr%3A%3ANonNull%3A%3Adangling"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "On top of these basic layout requirements, a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " must point to a valid value of ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "So long as ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "T: Sized",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is guaranteed to be represented",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "as a single pointer and is also ABI-compatible with C pointers",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "(i.e. the C type ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "T*",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "). This means that if you have extern \"C\"",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Rust functions that will be called from C, you can define those",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Rust functions using ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " types, and use ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "T*",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " as corresponding",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "type on the C side. As an example, consider this C header which",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "declares functions that create and destroy some kind of ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Foo",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "value:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "c",
                "code": "/* C header */\n\n/* Returns ownership to the caller */\nstruct Foo* foo_new(void);\n\n/* Takes ownership from the caller; no-op when invoked with null */\nvoid foo_delete(struct Foo*);\n"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "These two functions might be implemented in Rust as follows. Here, the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "struct Foo*",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " type from C is translated to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box<Foo>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", which captures",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the ownership constraints. Note also that the nullable argument to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "foo_delete",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is represented in Rust as ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Option<Box<Foo>>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", since ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box<Foo>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "cannot be null.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "#[repr(C)]\npub struct Foo;\n\n#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\npub extern \"C\" fn foo_new() -> Box<Foo> {\n    Box::new(Foo)\n}\n\n#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\npub extern \"C\" fn foo_delete(_: Option<Box<Foo>>) {}"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Even though ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " has the same representation and C ABI as a C pointer,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "this does not mean that you can convert an arbitrary ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "T*",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " into a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "and expect things to work. ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " values will always be fully aligned,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "non-null pointers. Moreover, the destructor for ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " will attempt to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "free the value with the global allocator. In general, the best practice",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "is to only use ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " for pointers that originated from the global",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "allocator.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Important.",
                    "style": "Strong"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " At least at present, you should avoid using",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " types for functions that are defined in C but invoked",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "from Rust. In those cases, you should directly mirror the C types",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "as closely as possible. Using types like ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " where the C",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "definition is just using ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "T*",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " can lead to undefined behavior, as",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "described in ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "rust-lang/unsafe-code-guidelines#198",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/unsafe-code-guidelines/issues/198"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Considerations for unsafe code",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Warning: This section is not normative and is subject to change, possibly",
                    "style": "Strong"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "being relaxed in the future! It is a simplified summary of the rules",
                    "style": "Strong"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "currently implemented in the compiler.",
                    "style": "Strong"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The aliasing rules for ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " are the same as for ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&mut T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "asserts uniqueness over its content. Using raw pointers derived from a box",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "after that box has been mutated through, moved or borrowed as ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&mut T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "is not allowed. For more guidance on working with box from unsafe code, see",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "rust-lang/unsafe-code-guidelines#326",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/unsafe-code-guidelines/issues/326"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Editions",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "A special case exists for the implementation of ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "IntoIterator",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " for arrays on the Rust 2021",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "edition, as documented ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "here",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3Aarray"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". Unfortunately, it was later found that a similar",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "workaround should be added for boxed slices, and this was applied in the 2024 edition.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Specifically, ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "IntoIterator",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is implemented for ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box<[T]>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " on all editions, but specific calls",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "into_iter()",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " for boxed slices will defer to the slice implementation on editions before",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "2024:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "// Rust 2015, 2018, and 2021:\n\nlet boxed_slice: Box<[i32]> = vec![0; 3].into_boxed_slice();\n\n// This creates a slice iterator, producing references to each value.\nfor item in boxed_slice.into_iter().enumerate() {\n    let (i, x): (usize, &i32) = item;\n    println!(\"boxed_slice[{i}] = {x}\");\n}\n\n// The `boxed_slice_into_iter` lint suggests this change for future compatibility:\nfor item in boxed_slice.iter().enumerate() {\n    let (i, x): (usize, &i32) = item;\n    println!(\"boxed_slice[{i}] = {x}\");\n}\n\n// You can explicitly iterate a boxed slice by value using `IntoIterator::into_iter`\nfor item in IntoIterator::into_iter(boxed_slice).enumerate() {\n    let (i, x): (usize, i32) = item;\n    println!(\"boxed_slice[{i}] = {x}\");\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Similar to the array implementation, this may be modified in the future to remove this override,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "and it's best to avoid relying on this edition-dependent behavior if you wish to preserve",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "compatibility with future versions of the compiler.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "fmt",
        "kind": "module",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/fmt/index.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Utilities for formatting and printing ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "String",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "s.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This module contains the runtime support for the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "format!",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/macro.format.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " syntax extension.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "This macro is implemented in the compiler to emit calls to this module in",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "order to format arguments at runtime into strings.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Usage",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "format!",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/macro.format.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " macro is intended to be familiar to those coming from C's",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "printf",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "/",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "fprintf",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " functions or Python's ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "str.format",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " function.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Some examples of the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "format!",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/macro.format.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " extension are:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "format!(\"Hello\");                 // => \"Hello\"\nformat!(\"Hello, {}!\", \"world\");   // => \"Hello, world!\"\nformat!(\"The number is {}\", 1);   // => \"The number is 1\"\nformat!(\"{:?}\", (3, 4));          // => \"(3, 4)\"\nformat!(\"{value}\", value=4);      // => \"4\"\nlet people = \"Rustaceans\";\nformat!(\"Hello {people}!\");       // => \"Hello Rustaceans!\"\nformat!(\"{} {}\", 1, 2);           // => \"1 2\"\nformat!(\"{:04}\", 42);             // => \"0042\" with leading zeros\nformat!(\"{:#?}\", (100, 200));     // => \"(\n                                  //       100,\n                                  //       200,\n                                  //     )\""
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "From these, you can see that the first argument is a format string. It is",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "required by the compiler for this to be a string literal; it cannot be a",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "variable passed in (in order to perform validity checking). The compiler",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "will then parse the format string and determine if the list of arguments",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "provided is suitable to pass to this format string.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "To convert a single value to a string, use the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "to_string",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " method. This",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "will use the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Display",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/fmt/index.html?search=core%3A%3Afmt%3A%3ADisplay"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " formatting trait.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Positional parameters",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Each formatting argument is allowed to specify which value argument it's",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "referencing, and if omitted it is assumed to be \"the next argument\". For",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "example, the format string ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "{} {} {}",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " would take three parameters, and they",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "would be formatted in the same order as they're given. The format string",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "{2} {1} {0}",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", however, would format arguments in reverse order.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Things can get a little tricky once you start intermingling the two types of",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "positional specifiers. The \"next argument\" specifier can be thought of as an",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "iterator over the argument. Each time a \"next argument\" specifier is seen,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the iterator advances. This leads to behavior like this:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "format!(\"{1} {} {0} {}\", 1, 2); // => \"2 1 1 2\""
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The internal iterator over the argument has not been advanced by the time",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the first ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "{}",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is seen, so it prints the first argument. Then upon reaching",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the second ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "{}",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", the iterator has advanced forward to the second argument.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Essentially, parameters that explicitly name their argument do not affect",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "parameters that do not name an argument in terms of positional specifiers.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "A format string is required to use all of its arguments, otherwise it is a",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "compile-time error. You may refer to the same argument more than once in the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "format string.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Named parameters",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Rust itself does not have a Python-like equivalent of named parameters to a",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "function, but the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "format!",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/macro.format.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " macro is a syntax extension that allows it to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "leverage named parameters. Named parameters are listed at the end of the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "argument list and have the syntax:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "text",
                "code": "identifier '=' expression\n"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "For example, the following ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "format!",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/macro.format.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " expressions all use named arguments:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "format!(\"{argument}\", argument = \"test\");   // => \"test\"\nformat!(\"{name} {}\", 1, name = 2);          // => \"2 1\"\nformat!(\"{a} {c} {b}\", a=\"a\", b='b', c=3);  // => \"a 3 b\""
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "If a named parameter does not appear in the argument list, ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "format!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " will",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "reference a variable with that name in the current scope.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let argument = 2 + 2;\nformat!(\"{argument}\");   // => \"4\"\n\nfn make_string(a: u32, b: &str) -> String {\n    format!(\"{b} {a}\")\n}\nmake_string(927, \"label\"); // => \"label 927\""
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "It is not valid to put positional parameters (those without names) after",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "arguments that have names. Like with positional parameters, it is not",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "valid to provide named parameters that are unused by the format string.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Formatting Parameters",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Each argument being formatted can be transformed by a number of formatting",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "parameters (corresponding to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "format_spec",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " in ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the syntax",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "#syntax"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "). These",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "parameters affect the string representation of what's being formatted.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The colon ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ":",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " in format syntax divides identifier of the input data and",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the formatting options, the colon itself does not change anything, only",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "introduces the options.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let a = 5;\nlet b = &a;\nprintln!(\"{a:e} {b:p}\"); // => 5e0 0x7ffe37b7273c"
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Width",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "// All of these print \"Hello x    !\"\nprintln!(\"Hello {:5}!\", \"x\");\nprintln!(\"Hello {:1$}!\", \"x\", 5);\nprintln!(\"Hello {1:0$}!\", 5, \"x\");\nprintln!(\"Hello {:width$}!\", \"x\", width = 5);\nlet width = 5;\nprintln!(\"Hello {:width$}!\", \"x\");"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This is a parameter for the \"minimum width\" that the format should take up.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "If the value's string does not fill up this many characters, then the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "padding specified by fill/alignment will be used to take up the required",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "space (see below).",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The width can also be provided dynamically by referencing another argument",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "with a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "$",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " suffix. Use ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "{:N$}",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " to reference the Nth positional argument",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "(where N is an integer), or ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "{:name$}",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " to reference a named argument. The",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "referenced argument must be of type ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "usize",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3Ausize"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Referring to an argument with the dollar syntax does not affect the \"next",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "argument\" counter, so it's usually a good idea to refer to arguments by",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "position, or use named arguments.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Fill/Alignment",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "assert_eq!(format!(\"Hello {:<5}!\", \"x\"),  \"Hello x    !\");\nassert_eq!(format!(\"Hello {:-<5}!\", \"x\"), \"Hello x----!\");\nassert_eq!(format!(\"Hello {:^5}!\", \"x\"),  \"Hello   x  !\");\nassert_eq!(format!(\"Hello {:>5}!\", \"x\"),  \"Hello     x!\");"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The optional fill character and alignment is provided normally in conjunction with the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "width",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "#width"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " parameter. It must be defined before ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "width",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", right after the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ":",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "This indicates that if the value being formatted is smaller than",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "width",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " some extra characters will be printed around it.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Filling comes in the following variants for different alignments:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "[fill]<",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " - the argument is left-aligned in ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "width",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " columns",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "[fill]^",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " - the argument is center-aligned in ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "width",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " columns",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "[fill]>",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " - the argument is right-aligned in ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "width",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " columns",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The default ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "fill/alignment",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "#fillalignment"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " for non-numerics is a space and",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "left-aligned. The",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "default for numeric formatters is also a space character but with right-alignment. If",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "0",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " flag (see below) is specified for numerics, then the implicit fill character is",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "0",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Note that alignment might not be implemented by some types. In particular, it",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "is not generally implemented for the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Debug",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " trait.  A good way to ensure",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "padding is applied is to format your input, then pad this resulting string",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "to obtain your output:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "println!(\"Hello {:^15}!\", format!(\"{:?}\", Some(\"hi\"))); // => \"Hello   Some(\"hi\")   !\""
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Sign/",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "#",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "/",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "0",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "assert_eq!(format!(\"Hello {:+}!\", 5), \"Hello +5!\");\nassert_eq!(format!(\"{:#x}!\", 27), \"0x1b!\");\nassert_eq!(format!(\"Hello {:05}!\", 5),  \"Hello 00005!\");\nassert_eq!(format!(\"Hello {:05}!\", -5), \"Hello -0005!\");\nassert_eq!(format!(\"{:#010x}!\", 27), \"0x0000001b!\");"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "These are all flags altering the behavior of the formatter.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "+",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " - This is intended for numeric types and indicates that the sign",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "should always be printed. By default only the negative sign of signed values",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "is printed, and the sign of positive or unsigned values is omitted.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "This flag indicates that the correct sign (",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "+",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " or ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "-",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ") should always be printed.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "-",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " - Currently not used",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "#",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " - This flag indicates that the \"alternate\" form of printing should",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "be used. The alternate forms are:",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "list",
                        "items": [
                          {
                            "content": [
                              {
                                "type": "paragraph",
                                "spans": [
                                  {
                                    "text": "#?",
                                    "style": "InlineCode"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": " - pretty-print the ",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": "Debug",
                                    "style": "InlineCode",
                                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/fmt/index.html?search=core%3A%3Afmt%3A%3ADebug"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": " formatting (adds linebreaks and indentation)",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  }
                                ]
                              }
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "content": [
                              {
                                "type": "paragraph",
                                "spans": [
                                  {
                                    "text": "#x",
                                    "style": "InlineCode"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": " - precedes the argument with a ",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": "0x",
                                    "style": "InlineCode"
                                  }
                                ]
                              }
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "content": [
                              {
                                "type": "paragraph",
                                "spans": [
                                  {
                                    "text": "#X",
                                    "style": "InlineCode"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": " - precedes the argument with a ",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": "0x",
                                    "style": "InlineCode"
                                  }
                                ]
                              }
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "content": [
                              {
                                "type": "paragraph",
                                "spans": [
                                  {
                                    "text": "#b",
                                    "style": "InlineCode"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": " - precedes the argument with a ",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": "0b",
                                    "style": "InlineCode"
                                  }
                                ]
                              }
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "content": [
                              {
                                "type": "paragraph",
                                "spans": [
                                  {
                                    "text": "#o",
                                    "style": "InlineCode"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": " - precedes the argument with a ",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": "0o",
                                    "style": "InlineCode"
                                  }
                                ]
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "See ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Formatting traits",
                            "style": "Plain",
                            "url": "#formatting-traits"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " for a description of what the ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "?",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ", ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "x",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ", ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "X",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ",",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "b",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ", and ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "o",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " flags do.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "0",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " - This is used to indicate for integer formats that the padding to ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "width",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " should",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "both be done with a ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "0",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " character as well as be sign-aware. A format",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "like ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "{:08}",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " would yield ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "00000001",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " for the integer ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "1",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ", while the",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "same format would yield ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "-0000001",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " for the integer ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "-1",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ". Notice that",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "the negative version has one fewer zero than the positive version.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Note that padding zeros are always placed after the sign (if any)",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "and before the digits. When used together with the ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "#",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " flag, a similar",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "rule applies: padding zeros are inserted after the prefix but before",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "the digits. The prefix is included in the total width.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "This flag overrides the ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "fill character and alignment flag",
                            "style": "Plain",
                            "url": "#fillalignment"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ".",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Precision",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "For non-numeric types, this can be considered a \"maximum width\". If the resulting string is",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "longer than this width, then it is truncated down to this many characters and that truncated",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "value is emitted with proper ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "fill",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "alignment",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "width",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " if those parameters are set.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "For integral types, this is ignored.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "For floating-point types, this indicates how many digits after the decimal point should be",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "printed.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "There are three possible ways to specify the desired ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "precision",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ":",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "An integer ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ".N",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ":",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "the integer ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "N",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " itself is the precision.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "An integer or name followed by dollar sign ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ".N$",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ":",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "use the value of format ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "argument",
                            "style": "Emphasis"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "N",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " (which must be a ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "usize",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ") as the precision.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "An integer refers to a positional argument, and a name refers to a named argument.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "An asterisk ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ".*",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ":",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": ".*",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " means that this ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "{...}",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " is associated with ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "two",
                            "style": "Emphasis"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " format inputs rather than one:",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "list",
                        "items": [
                          {
                            "content": [
                              {
                                "type": "paragraph",
                                "spans": [
                                  {
                                    "text": "If a format string in the fashion of ",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": "{:<spec>.*}",
                                    "style": "InlineCode"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": " is used, then the first input holds",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": " ",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": "the ",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": "usize",
                                    "style": "InlineCode"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": " precision, and the second holds the value to print.",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  }
                                ]
                              }
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "content": [
                              {
                                "type": "paragraph",
                                "spans": [
                                  {
                                    "text": "If a format string in the fashion of ",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": "{<arg>:<spec>.*}",
                                    "style": "InlineCode"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": " is used, then the ",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": "<arg>",
                                    "style": "InlineCode"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": " part",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": " ",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": "refers to the value to print, and the ",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": "precision",
                                    "style": "InlineCode"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": " is taken like it was specified with an",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": " ",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": "omitted positional parameter (",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": "{}",
                                    "style": "InlineCode"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": " instead of ",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": "{<arg>:}",
                                    "style": "InlineCode"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": ").",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  }
                                ]
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "For example, the following calls all print the same thing ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Hello x is 0.01000",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ":",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "// Hello {arg 0 (\"x\")} is {arg 1 (0.01) with precision specified inline (5)}\nprintln!(\"Hello {0} is {1:.5}\", \"x\", 0.01);\n\n// Hello {arg 1 (\"x\")} is {arg 2 (0.01) with precision specified in arg 0 (5)}\nprintln!(\"Hello {1} is {2:.0$}\", 5, \"x\", 0.01);\n\n// Hello {arg 0 (\"x\")} is {arg 2 (0.01) with precision specified in arg 1 (5)}\nprintln!(\"Hello {0} is {2:.1$}\", \"x\", 5, 0.01);\n\n// Hello {next arg -> arg 0 (\"x\")} is {second of next two args -> arg 2 (0.01) with precision\n//                          specified in first of next two args -> arg 1 (5)}\nprintln!(\"Hello {} is {:.*}\",    \"x\", 5, 0.01);\n\n// Hello {arg 1 (\"x\")} is {arg 2 (0.01) with precision\n//                          specified in next arg -> arg 0 (5)}\nprintln!(\"Hello {1} is {2:.*}\",  5, \"x\", 0.01);\n\n// Hello {next arg -> arg 0 (\"x\")} is {arg 2 (0.01) with precision\n//                          specified in next arg -> arg 1 (5)}\nprintln!(\"Hello {} is {2:.*}\",   \"x\", 5, 0.01);\n\n// Hello {next arg -> arg 0 (\"x\")} is {arg \"number\" (0.01) with precision specified\n//                          in arg \"prec\" (5)}\nprintln!(\"Hello {} is {number:.prec$}\", \"x\", prec = 5, number = 0.01);"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "While these:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "println!(\"{}, `{name:.*}` has 3 fractional digits\", \"Hello\", 3, name=1234.56);\nprintln!(\"{}, `{name:.*}` has 3 characters\", \"Hello\", 3, name=\"1234.56\");\nprintln!(\"{}, `{name:>8.*}` has 3 right-aligned characters\", \"Hello\", 3, name=\"1234.56\");"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "print three significantly different things:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "text",
                "code": "Hello, `1234.560` has 3 fractional digits\nHello, `123` has 3 characters\nHello, `     123` has 3 right-aligned characters\n"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "When truncating these values, Rust uses ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "round half-to-even",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rounding#Rounding_half_to_even"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ",",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "which is the default rounding mode in IEEE 754.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "For example,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "print!(\"{0:.1$e}\", 12345, 3);\nprint!(\"{0:.1$e}\", 12355, 3);"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Would return:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "text",
                "code": "1.234e4\n1.236e4\n"
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Localization",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "In some programming languages, the behavior of string formatting functions",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "depends on the operating system's locale setting. The format functions",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "provided by Rust's standard library do not have any concept of locale and",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "will produce the same results on all systems regardless of user",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "configuration.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "For example, the following code will always print ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "1.5",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " even if the system",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "locale uses a decimal separator other than a dot.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "println!(\"The value is {}\", 1.5);"
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Escaping",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The literal characters ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "{",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "}",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " may be included in a string by preceding",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "them with the same character. For example, the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "{",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " character is escaped with",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "{{",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "}",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " character is escaped with ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "}}",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "assert_eq!(format!(\"Hello {{}}\"), \"Hello {}\");\nassert_eq!(format!(\"{{ Hello\"), \"{ Hello\");"
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Syntax",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "To summarize, here you can find the full grammar of format strings.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "The syntax for the formatting language used is drawn from other languages,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "so it should not be too alien. Arguments are formatted with Python-like",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "syntax, meaning that arguments are surrounded by ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "{}",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " instead of the C-like",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "%",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". The actual grammar for the formatting syntax is:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "text",
                "code": "format_string := text [ maybe_format text ] *\nmaybe_format := '{' '{' | '}' '}' | format\nformat := '{' [ argument ] [ ':' format_spec ] [ ws ] * '}'\nargument := integer | identifier\n\nformat_spec := [[fill]align][sign]['#']['0'][width]['.' precision][type]\nfill := character\nalign := '<' | '^' | '>'\nsign := '+' | '-'\nwidth := count\nprecision := count | '*'\ntype := '?' | 'x?' | 'X?' | 'o' | 'x' | 'X' | 'p' | 'b' | 'e' | 'E'\ncount := parameter | integer\nparameter := argument '$'\n"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "In the above grammar,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "text",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " must not contain any ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "'{'",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " or ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "'}'",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " characters,",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "ws",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " is any character for which ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "char::is_whitespace",
                            "style": "InlineCode",
                            "url": "https://docs.rs/char/latest/char/index.html?search=char%3A%3Ais%5Fwhitespace"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " returns ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "true",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ", has no semantic",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "meaning and is completely optional,",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "integer",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " is a decimal integer that may contain leading zeroes and must fit into an ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "usize",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " and",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "identifier",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " is an ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "IDENTIFIER_OR_KEYWORD",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " (not an ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "IDENTIFIER",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ") as",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "defined by the ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Rust language",
                            "style": "Plain",
                            "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/identifiers.html"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain",
                            "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/identifiers.html"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "reference",
                            "style": "Plain",
                            "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/identifiers.html"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ", except",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "for a bare ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "_",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ".",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Formatting traits",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "When requesting that an argument be formatted with a particular type, you",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "are actually requesting that an argument ascribes to a particular trait.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "This allows multiple actual types to be formatted via ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "{:x}",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " (like ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "i8",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3Ai8"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " as",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "well as ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "isize",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3Aisize"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "). The current mapping of types to traits is:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "nothing",
                            "style": "Emphasis"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ⇒ ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Display",
                            "style": "InlineCode",
                            "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/fmt/index.html?search=core%3A%3Afmt%3A%3ADisplay"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "?",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ⇒ ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Debug",
                            "style": "InlineCode",
                            "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/fmt/index.html?search=core%3A%3Afmt%3A%3ADebug"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
