      {
        "path": "matches",
        "kind": "macro",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.matches.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Returns whether the given expression matches the provided pattern.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The pattern syntax is exactly the same as found in a match arm. The optional if guard can be",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "used to add additional checks that must be true for the matched value, otherwise this macro will",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "return ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "false",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "When testing that a value matches a pattern, it's generally preferable to use",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "assert_matches!",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macros/macro.assert_matches.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " as it will print the debug representation of the value if the assertion",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "fails.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let foo = 'f';\nassert!(matches!(foo, 'A'..='Z' | 'a'..='z'));\n\nlet bar = Some(4);\nassert!(matches!(bar, Some(x) if x > 2));"
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "primitive",
        "kind": "module",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/primitive/index.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This module reexports the primitive types to allow usage that is not",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "possibly shadowed by other declared types.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This is normally only useful in macro generated code.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "An example of this is when generating a new struct and an impl for it:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "pub struct bool;\n\nimpl QueryId for bool {\n    const SOME_PROPERTY: bool = true;\n}\n"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Note that the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "SOME_PROPERTY",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " associated constant would not compile, as its",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "type ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "bool",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " refers to the struct, rather than to the primitive bool type.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "A correct implementation could look like:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "pub struct bool;\n\nimpl QueryId for bool {\n    const SOME_PROPERTY: ::core::primitive::bool = true;\n}\n"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "We also used ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "::core",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " instead of ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "core",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", because ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "core",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " can be",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "shadowed, too. Paths, starting with ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "::",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", are searched in",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "extern prelude",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/reference/names/preludes.html#extern-prelude"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " since Edition 2018.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "todo",
        "kind": "macro",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.todo.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Indicates unfinished code.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This can be useful if you are prototyping and just",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "want a placeholder to let your code pass type analysis.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The difference between ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "unimplemented!",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.unimplemented.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "todo!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is that while ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "todo!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " conveys",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "an intent of implementing the functionality later and the message is \"not yet",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "implemented\", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "unimplemented!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " makes no such claims. Its message is \"not implemented\".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Also, some IDEs will mark ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "todo!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "s.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Panics",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This will always ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "panic!",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.panic.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " because ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "todo!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is just a shorthand for ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "panic!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " with a",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "fixed, specific message.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Like ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "panic!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", this macro has a second form for displaying custom values.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Here's an example of some in-progress code. We have a trait ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Foo",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ":",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "trait Foo {\n    fn bar(&self) -> u8;\n    fn baz(&self);\n    fn qux(&self) -> Result<u64, ()>;\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "We want to implement ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Foo",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " on one of our types, but we also want to work on",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "just ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "bar()",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " first. In order for our code to compile, we need to implement",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "baz()",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "qux()",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", so we can use ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "todo!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ":",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "struct MyStruct;\n\nimpl Foo for MyStruct {\n    fn bar(&self) -> u8 {\n        1 + 1\n    }\n\n    fn baz(&self) {\n        // Let's not worry about implementing baz() for now\n        todo!();\n    }\n\n    fn qux(&self) -> Result<u64, ()> {\n        // We can add a message to todo! to display our omission.\n        // This will display:\n        // \"thread 'main' panicked at 'not yet implemented: MyStruct is not yet quxable'\".\n        todo!(\"MyStruct is not yet quxable\");\n    }\n}\n\nfn main() {\n    let s = MyStruct;\n    s.bar();\n\n    // We aren't even using baz() or qux(), so this is fine.\n}"
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "assert",
        "kind": "macro",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.assert.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Asserts that a boolean expression is ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "true",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " at runtime.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This will invoke the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "panic!",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.panic.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " macro if the provided expression cannot be",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "evaluated to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "true",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " at runtime.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Uses",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Assertions are always checked in both debug and release builds, and cannot",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "be disabled. See ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "debug_assert!",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.debug_assert.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " for assertions that are not enabled in",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "release builds by default.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Unsafe code may rely on ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "assert!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " to enforce run-time invariants that, if",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "violated could lead to unsafety.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Other use-cases of ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "assert!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " include testing and enforcing run-time",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "invariants in safe code (whose violation cannot result in unsafety).",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Custom Messages",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This macro has a second form, where a custom panic message can",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "be provided with or without arguments for formatting. See ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "std::fmt",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/../std/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2E%3A%3Astd%3A%3Afmt"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "for syntax for this form. Expressions used as format arguments will only",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "be evaluated if the assertion fails.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "// the panic message for these assertions is the stringified value of the\n// expression given.\nassert!(true);\n\nfn some_computation() -> bool {\n    // Some expensive computation here\n    true\n}\n\nassert!(some_computation());\n\n// assert with a custom message\nlet x = true;\nassert!(x, \"x wasn't true!\");\n\nlet a = 3; let b = 27;\nassert!(a + b == 30, \"a = {}, b = {}\", a, b);"
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "cfg",
        "kind": "macro",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.cfg.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Evaluates boolean combinations of configuration flags at compile-time.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "In addition to the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "#[cfg]",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " attribute, this macro is provided to allow",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "boolean expression evaluation of configuration flags. This frequently",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "leads to less duplicated code.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The syntax given to this macro is the same syntax as the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "cfg",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2Freference%2Fconditional%2Dcompilation"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "attribute.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "cfg!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", unlike ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "#[cfg]",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", does not remove any code and only evaluates to true or false. For",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "example, all blocks in an if/else expression need to be valid when ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "cfg!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is used for",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the condition, regardless of what ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "cfg!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is evaluating.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let my_directory = if cfg!(windows) {\n    \"windows-specific-directory\"\n} else {\n    \"unix-directory\"\n};"
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "column",
        "kind": "macro",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.column.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Expands to the column number at which it was invoked.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "With ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "line!",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.line.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "file!",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.file.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", these macros provide debugging information for",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "developers about the location within the source.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The expanded expression has type ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "u32",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and is 1-based, so the first column",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "in each line evaluates to 1, the second to 2, etc. This is consistent",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "with error messages by common compilers or popular editors.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "The returned column is ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "not necessarily",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " the line of the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "column!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " invocation itself,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "but rather the first macro invocation leading up to the invocation",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "of the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "column!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " macro.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let current_col = column!();\nprintln!(\"defined on column: {current_col}\");"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "column!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " counts Unicode code points, not bytes or graphemes. As a result, the first two",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "invocations return the same value, but the third does not.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let a = (\"foobar\", column!()).1;\nlet b = (\"人之初性本善\", column!()).1;\nlet c = (\"f̅o̅o̅b̅a̅r̅\", column!()).1; // Uses combining overline (U+0305)\n\nassert_eq!(a, b);\nassert_ne!(b, c);"
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "compile_error",
        "kind": "macro",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.compile_error.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Causes compilation to fail with the given error message when encountered.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This macro should be used when a crate uses a conditional compilation strategy to provide",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "better error messages for erroneous conditions. It's the compiler-level form of ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "panic!",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.panic.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ",",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "but emits an error during ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "compilation",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " rather than at ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "runtime",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Two such examples are macros and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "#[cfg]",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " environments.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Emit a better compiler error if a macro is passed invalid values. Without the final branch,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the compiler would still emit an error, but the error's message would not mention the two",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "valid values.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "macro_rules! give_me_foo_or_bar {\n    (foo) => {};\n    (bar) => {};\n    ($x:ident) => {\n        compile_error!(\"This macro only accepts `foo` or `bar`\");\n    }\n}\n\ngive_me_foo_or_bar!(neither);\n// ^ will fail at compile time with message \"This macro only accepts `foo` or `bar`\""
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Emit a compiler error if one of a number of features isn't available.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "#[cfg(not(any(feature = \"foo\", feature = \"bar\")))]\ncompile_error!(\"Either feature \\\"foo\\\" or \\\"bar\\\" must be enabled for this crate.\");"
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "concat",
        "kind": "macro",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.concat.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Concatenates literals into a static string slice.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This macro takes any number of comma-separated literals, yielding an",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "expression of type ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&'static str",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " which represents all of the literals",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "concatenated left-to-right.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Integer and floating point literals are ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "stringified",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.stringify.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " in order to be",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "concatenated.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let s = concat!(\"test\", 10, 'b', true);\nassert_eq!(s, \"test10btrue\");"
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "const_format_args",
        "kind": "macro",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.const_format_args.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
