      },
      {
        "path": "env",
        "kind": "macro",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.env.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Inspects an environment variable at compile time.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This macro will expand to the value of the named environment variable at",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "compile time, yielding an expression of type ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&'static str",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". Use",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "std::env::var",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2Fstd%2Fenv%2Ffn%2Evar"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " instead if you want to read the value at runtime.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "If the environment variable is not defined, then a compilation error",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "will be emitted. To not emit a compile error, use the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "option_env!",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.option_env.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "macro instead. A compilation error will also be emitted if the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "environment variable is not a valid Unicode string.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let path: &'static str = env!(\"PATH\");\nprintln!(\"the $PATH variable at the time of compiling was: {path}\");"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "You can customize the error message by passing a string as the second",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "parameter:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let doc: &'static str = env!(\"documentation\", \"what's that?!\");"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "If the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "documentation",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " environment variable is not defined, you'll get",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the following error:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "text",
                "code": "error: what's that?!\n"
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "file",
        "kind": "macro",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.file.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Expands to the file name in which it was invoked.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "With ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "line!",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.line.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "column!",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.column.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", these macros provide debugging information for",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "developers about the location within the source.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The expanded expression has type ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&'static str",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", and the returned file",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "is not the invocation of the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "file!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " macro itself, but rather the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "first macro invocation leading up to the invocation of the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "file!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "macro.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The file name is derived from the crate root's source path passed to the Rust compiler",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "and the sequence the compiler takes to get from the crate root to the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "module containing ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "file!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", modified by any flags passed to the Rust compiler (e.g.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "--remap-path-prefix",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ").  If the crate's source path is relative, the initial base",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "directory will be the working directory of the Rust compiler.  For example, if the source",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "path passed to the compiler is ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "./src/lib.rs",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " which has a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "mod foo;",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " with a source path of",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "src/foo/mod.rs",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", then calling ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "file!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " inside ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "mod foo;",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " will return ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "./src/foo/mod.rs",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Future compiler options might make further changes to the behavior of ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "file!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ",",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "including potentially making it entirely empty. Code (e.g. test libraries)",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "relying on ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "file!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " producing an openable file path would be incompatible",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "with such options, and might wish to recommend not using those options.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
