      {
        "path": "include",
        "kind": "macro",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.include.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Parses a file as an expression or an item according to the context.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Warning",
                    "style": "Strong"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ": For multi-file Rust projects, the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "include!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " macro is probably not what you",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "are looking for. Usually, multi-file Rust projects use",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "modules",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/items/modules.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". Multi-file projects and",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "modules are explained in the Rust-by-Example book",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "here",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/rust-by-example/mod/split.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and the module system is",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "explained in the Rust Book",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "here",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch07-02-defining-modules-to-control-scope-and-privacy.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The included file is placed in the surrounding code",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "unhygienically",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/macros-by-example.html#hygiene"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". If",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the included file is parsed as an expression and variables or functions share names across",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "both files, it could result in variables or functions being different from what the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "included file expected.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The included file is located relative to the current file (similarly to how modules are",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "found). The provided path is interpreted in a platform-specific way at compile time. So,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "for instance, an invocation with a Windows path containing backslashes ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "\\",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " would not",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "compile correctly on Unix.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Uses",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "include!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " macro is primarily used for two purposes. It is used to include",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "documentation that is written in a separate file and it is used to include ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "build artifacts",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/build-scripts.html#outputs-of-the-build-script"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/build-scripts.html#outputs-of-the-build-script"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "usually as a result from the ",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/build-scripts.html#outputs-of-the-build-script"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "build.rs",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/build-scripts.html#outputs-of-the-build-script"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/build-scripts.html#outputs-of-the-build-script"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "script",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/build-scripts.html#outputs-of-the-build-script"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "When using the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "include",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " macro to include stretches of documentation, remember that the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "included file still needs to be a valid Rust syntax. It is also possible to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "use the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "include_str",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.include_str.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " macro as ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "#![doc = include_str!(\"...\")]",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " (at the module level) or",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "#[doc = include_str!(\"...\")]",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " (at the item level) to include documentation from a plain",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "text or markdown file.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Assume there are two files in the same directory with the following contents:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "File 'monkeys.in':",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "ignore (only-for-syntax-highlight)",
                "code": "['🙈', '🙊', '🙉']\n    .iter()\n    .cycle()\n    .take(6)\n    .collect::<String>()\n"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "File 'main.rs':",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "ignore (cannot-doctest-external-file-dependency)",
                "code": "fn main() {\n    let my_string = include!(\"monkeys.in\");\n    assert_eq!(\"🙈🙊🙉🙈🙊🙉\", my_string);\n    println!(\"{my_string}\");\n}\n"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Compiling 'main.rs' and running the resulting binary will print",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "\"🙈🙊🙉🙈🙊🙉\".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "include_bytes",
        "kind": "macro",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.include_bytes.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Includes a file as a reference to a byte array.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The file is located relative to the current file (similarly to how",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "modules are found). The provided path is interpreted in a platform-specific",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "way at compile time. So, for instance, an invocation with a Windows path",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "containing backslashes ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "\\",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " would not compile correctly on Unix.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This macro will yield an expression of type ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&'static [u8; N]",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " which is",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the contents of the file.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Assume there are two files in the same directory with the following",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "contents:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "File 'spanish.in':",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "text",
                "code": "adiós\n"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "File 'main.rs':",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "ignore (cannot-doctest-external-file-dependency)",
                "code": "fn main() {\n    let bytes = include_bytes!(\"spanish.in\");\n    assert_eq!(bytes, b\"adi\\xc3\\xb3s\\n\");\n    print!(\"{}\", String::from_utf8_lossy(bytes));\n}\n"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Compiling 'main.rs' and running the resulting binary will print \"adiós\".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
