              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Unlike ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "assert!",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.assert.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "debug_assert!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " statements are only enabled in non",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "optimized builds by default. An optimized build will not execute",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "debug_assert!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " statements unless ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "-C debug-assertions",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is passed to the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "compiler. This makes ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "debug_assert!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " useful for checks that are too",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "expensive to be present in a release build but may be helpful during",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "development. The result of expanding ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "debug_assert!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is always type checked.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "An unchecked assertion allows a program in an inconsistent state to keep",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "running, which might have unexpected consequences but does not introduce",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "unsafety as long as this only happens in safe code. The performance cost",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "of assertions, however, is not measurable in general. Replacing ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "assert!",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.assert.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "with ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "debug_assert!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is thus only encouraged after thorough profiling, and",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "more importantly, only in safe code!",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "// the panic message for these assertions is the stringified value of the\n// expression given.\ndebug_assert!(true);\n\nfn some_expensive_computation() -> bool {\n    // Some expensive computation here\n    true\n}\ndebug_assert!(some_expensive_computation());\n\n// assert with a custom message\nlet x = true;\ndebug_assert!(x, \"x wasn't true!\");\n\nlet a = 3; let b = 27;\ndebug_assert!(a + b == 30, \"a = {}, b = {}\", a, b);"
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
