      {
        "path": "try",
        "kind": "macro",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.try.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Unwraps a result or propagates its error.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "?",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch09-02-recoverable-errors-with-result.html#a-shortcut-for-propagating-errors-the--operator"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " operator",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch09-02-recoverable-errors-with-result.html#a-shortcut-for-propagating-errors-the--operator"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " was added to replace ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "try!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "and should be used instead. Furthermore, ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "try",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is a reserved word",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "in Rust 2018, so if you must use it, you will need to use the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "raw-identifier syntax",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2Frust%2Dby%2Dexample%2Fcompatibility%2Fraw%5Fidentifiers"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ": ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "r#try",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "try!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " matches the given ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Result",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/result/enum.Result.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". In case of the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Ok",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " variant, the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "expression has the value of the wrapped value.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "In case of the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Err",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " variant, it retrieves the inner error. ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "try!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " then",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "performs conversion using ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "From",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". This provides automatic conversion",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "between specialized errors and more general ones. The resulting",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "error is then immediately returned.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Because of the early return, ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "try!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " can only be used in functions that",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "return ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Result",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/result/enum.Result.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "use std::io;\nuse std::fs::File;\nuse std::io::prelude::*;\n\nenum MyError {\n    FileWriteError\n}\n\nimpl From<io::Error> for MyError {\n    fn from(e: io::Error) -> MyError {\n        MyError::FileWriteError\n    }\n}\n\n// The preferred method of quick returning Errors\nfn write_to_file_question() -> Result<(), MyError> {\n    let mut file = File::create(\"my_best_friends.txt\")?;\n    file.write_all(b\"This is a list of my best friends.\")?;\n    Ok(())\n}\n\n// The previous method of quick returning Errors\nfn write_to_file_using_try() -> Result<(), MyError> {\n    let mut file = r#try!(File::create(\"my_best_friends.txt\"));\n    r#try!(file.write_all(b\"This is a list of my best friends.\"));\n    Ok(())\n}\n\n// This is equivalent to:\nfn write_to_file_using_match() -> Result<(), MyError> {\n    let mut file = r#try!(File::create(\"my_best_friends.txt\"));\n    match file.write_all(b\"This is a list of my best friends.\") {\n        Ok(v) => v,\n        Err(e) => return Err(From::from(e)),\n    }\n    Ok(())\n}"
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "unimplemented",
        "kind": "macro",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.unimplemented.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Indicates unimplemented code by panicking with a message of \"not implemented\".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This allows your code to type-check, which is useful if you are prototyping or",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "implementing a trait that requires multiple methods which you don't plan to use all of.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The difference between ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "unimplemented!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "todo!",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.todo.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is that while ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "todo!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "conveys an intent of implementing the functionality later and the message is \"not yet",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "implemented\", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "unimplemented!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " makes no such claims. Its message is \"not implemented\".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Also, some IDEs will mark ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "todo!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "s.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Panics",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This will always ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "panic!",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.panic.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " because ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "unimplemented!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is just a shorthand for ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "panic!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " with a",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "fixed, specific message.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Like ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "panic!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", this macro has a second form for displaying custom values.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Say we have a trait ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Foo",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ":",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "trait Foo {\n    fn bar(&self) -> u8;\n    fn baz(&self);\n    fn qux(&self) -> Result<u64, ()>;\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "We want to implement ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Foo",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " for 'MyStruct', but for some reason it only makes sense",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "to implement the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "bar()",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " function. ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "baz()",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "qux()",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " will still need to be defined",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "in our implementation of ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Foo",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", but we can use ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "unimplemented!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " in their definitions",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "to allow our code to compile.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "We still want to have our program stop running if the unimplemented methods are",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "reached.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "struct MyStruct;\n\nimpl Foo for MyStruct {\n    fn bar(&self) -> u8 {\n        1 + 1\n    }\n\n    fn baz(&self) {\n        // It makes no sense to `baz` a `MyStruct`, so we have no logic here\n        // at all.\n        // This will display \"thread 'main' panicked at 'not implemented'\".\n        unimplemented!();\n    }\n\n    fn qux(&self) -> Result<u64, ()> {\n        // We have some logic here,\n        // We can add a message to unimplemented! to display our omission.\n        // This will display:\n        // \"thread 'main' panicked at 'not implemented: MyStruct isn't quxable'\".\n        unimplemented!(\"MyStruct isn't quxable\");\n    }\n}\n\nfn main() {\n    let s = MyStruct;\n    s.bar();\n}"
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "unreachable",
        "kind": "macro",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/macro.unreachable.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
