      {
        "path": "dbg",
        "kind": "macro",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/macro.dbg.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Prints and returns the value of a given expression for quick and dirty",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "debugging.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "An example:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let a = 2;\nlet b = dbg!(a * 2) + 1;\n//      ^-- prints: [src/main.rs:2:9] a * 2 = 4\nassert_eq!(b, 5);"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The macro works by using the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Debug",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " implementation of the type of",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the given expression to print the value to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "stderr",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standard_streams#Standard_error_(stderr)"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " along with the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "source location of the macro invocation as well as the source code",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "of the expression.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Invoking the macro on an expression moves and takes ownership of it",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "before returning the evaluated expression unchanged. If the type",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "of the expression does not implement ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Copy",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and you don't want",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "to give up ownership, you can instead borrow with ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "dbg!(&expr)",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "for some expression ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "expr",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "dbg!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " macro works exactly the same in release builds.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "This is useful when debugging issues that only occur in release",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "builds or when debugging in release mode is significantly faster.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Note that the macro is intended as a debugging tool and therefore you",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "should avoid having uses of it in version control for long periods",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "(other than in tests and similar).",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Debug output from production code is better done with other facilities",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "such as the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "debug!",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://docs.rs/log/*/log/macro.debug.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " macro from the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "log",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://crates.io/crates/log"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " crate.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Stability",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The exact output printed by this macro should not be relied upon",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "and is subject to future changes.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Panics",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Panics if writing to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "io::stderr",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " fails.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Further examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "With a method call:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "fn foo(n: usize) {\n    if let Some(_) = dbg!(n.checked_sub(4)) {\n        // ...\n    }\n}\n\nfoo(3)"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This prints to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "stderr",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standard_streams#Standard_error_(stderr)"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ":",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "text",
                "code": "[src/main.rs:2:22] n.checked_sub(4) = None\n"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Naive factorial implementation:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "fn factorial(n: u32) -> u32 {\n    if dbg!(n <= 1) {\n        dbg!(1)\n    } else {\n        dbg!(n * factorial(n - 1))\n    }\n}\n\ndbg!(factorial(4));"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This prints to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "stderr",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standard_streams#Standard_error_(stderr)"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ":",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "text",
                "code": "[src/main.rs:2:8] n <= 1 = false\n[src/main.rs:2:8] n <= 1 = false\n[src/main.rs:2:8] n <= 1 = false\n[src/main.rs:2:8] n <= 1 = true\n[src/main.rs:3:9] 1 = 1\n[src/main.rs:7:9] n * factorial(n - 1) = 2\n[src/main.rs:7:9] n * factorial(n - 1) = 6\n[src/main.rs:7:9] n * factorial(n - 1) = 24\n[src/main.rs:9:1] factorial(4) = 24\n"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "dbg!(..)",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " macro moves the input:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "/// A wrapper around `usize` which importantly is not Copyable.\n#[derive(Debug)]\nstruct NoCopy(usize);\n\nlet a = NoCopy(42);\nlet _ = dbg!(a); // <-- `a` is moved here.\nlet _ = dbg!(a); // <-- `a` is moved again; error!"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "You can also use ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "dbg!()",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " without a value to just print the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "file and line whenever it's reached.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Finally, if you want to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "dbg!(..)",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " multiple values, it will treat them as",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "a tuple (and return it, too):",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "assert_eq!(dbg!(1usize, 2u32), (1, 2));"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "However, a single argument with a trailing comma will still not be treated",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "as a tuple, following the convention of ignoring trailing commas in macro",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "invocations. You can use a 1-tuple directly if you need one:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "assert_eq!(1, dbg!(1u32,)); // trailing comma ignored\nassert_eq!((1,), dbg!((1u32,))); // 1-tuple"
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "hash_map",
        "kind": "macro",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/macro.hash_map.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Creates a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "HashMap",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/collections/hash/map/struct.HashMap.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " containing the arguments.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "hash_map!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " allows specifying the entries that make",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "up the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "HashMap",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/collections/hash/map/struct.HashMap.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " where the key and value are separated by a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "=>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The entries are separated by commas with a trailing comma being allowed.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "It is semantically equivalent to using repeated ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "HashMap::insert",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/collections/hash/map/struct.HashMap.html#method.insert"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "on a newly created hashmap.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "hash_map!",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " will attempt to avoid repeated reallocations by",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "using ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "HashMap::with_capacity",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/collections/hash/map/struct.HashMap.html#method.with_capacity"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "#![feature(hash_map_macro)]\nuse std::hash_map;\n\nlet map = hash_map! {\n    \"key\" => \"value\",\n    \"key1\" => \"value1\"\n};\n\nassert_eq!(map.get(\"key\"), Some(&\"value\"));\nassert_eq!(map.get(\"key1\"), Some(&\"value1\"));\nassert!(map.get(\"brrrrrrooooommm\").is_none());"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "And with a trailing comma",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": " #![feature(hash_map_macro)]\n use std::hash_map;\n\n let map = hash_map! {\n     \"key\" => \"value\", // notice the ,\n };\n\n assert_eq!(map.get(\"key\"), Some(&\"value\"));"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The key and value are moved into the HashMap.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "thread_local",
        "kind": "macro",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/macro.thread_local.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Declare a new thread local storage key of type ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "std::thread::LocalKey",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/thread/local/struct.LocalKey.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Syntax",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The macro wraps any number of static declarations and makes them thread local.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Publicity and attributes for each static are allowed. Example:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "use std::cell::{Cell, RefCell};\n\nthread_local! {\n    pub static FOO: Cell<u32> = const { Cell::new(1) };\n\n    static BAR: RefCell<Vec<f32>> = RefCell::new(vec![1.0, 2.0]);\n}\n\nassert_eq!(FOO.get(), 1);\nBAR.with_borrow(|v| assert_eq!(v[1], 2.0));"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Note that only shared references (",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ") to the inner data may be obtained, so a",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "type such as ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cell",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cell/index.html?search=core%3A%3Acell%3A%3ACell"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " or ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "RefCell",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cell/index.html?search=core%3A%3Acell%3A%3ARefCell"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is typically used to allow mutating access.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This macro supports a special ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "const {}",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " syntax that can be used",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "when the initialization expression can be evaluated as a constant.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "This can enable a more efficient thread local implementation that",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "can avoid lazy initialization. For types that do not",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "need to be dropped",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/mem/index.html?search=core%3A%3Amem%3A%3Aneeds%5Fdrop"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", this can enable an",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "even more efficient implementation that does not need to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "track any additional state.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "use std::cell::RefCell;\n\nthread_local! {\n    pub static FOO: RefCell<Vec<u32>> = const { RefCell::new(Vec::new()) };\n}\n\nFOO.with_borrow(|v| assert_eq!(v.len(), 0));"
              },
