                  {
                    "text": "null_mut",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ptr/index.html?search=core%3A%3Aptr%3A%3Anull%5Fmut"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " functions to create null pointers, and the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "is_null",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://docs.rs/pointer/latest/pointer/index.html?search=pointer%3A%3Ais%5Fnull"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " method of the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "*const T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "*mut T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " types to check for null.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "The ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "*const T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "*mut T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " types also define the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "offset",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://docs.rs/pointer/latest/pointer/index.html?search=pointer%3A%3Aoffset"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " method, for",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "pointer math.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Common ways to create raw pointers",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "1. Coerce a reference (",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ") or mutable reference (",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&mut T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ").",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let my_num: i32 = 10;\nlet my_num_ptr: *const i32 = &my_num;\nlet mut my_speed: i32 = 88;\nlet my_speed_ptr: *mut i32 = &mut my_speed;"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "To get a pointer to a boxed value, dereference the box:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let my_num: Box<i32> = Box::new(10);\nlet my_num_ptr: *const i32 = &*my_num;\nlet mut my_speed: Box<i32> = Box::new(88);\nlet my_speed_ptr: *mut i32 = &mut *my_speed;"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This does not take ownership of the original allocation",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "and requires no resource management later,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "but you must not use the pointer after its lifetime.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "2. Consume a box (",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ").",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "into_raw",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/index.html?search=std%3A%3A%2E%2Fstd%2Fboxed%2Fstruct%2EBox"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " function consumes a box and returns",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the raw pointer. It doesn't destroy ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " or deallocate any memory.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let my_speed: Box<i32> = Box::new(88);\nlet my_speed: *mut i32 = Box::into_raw(my_speed);\n\n// By taking ownership of the original `Box<T>` though\n// we are obligated to put it together later to be destroyed.\nunsafe {\n    drop(Box::from_raw(my_speed));\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Note that here the call to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "drop",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/mem/index.html?search=core%3A%3Amem%3A%3Adrop"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is for clarity - it indicates",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "that we are done with the given value and it should be destroyed.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "3. Create it using ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&raw",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Instead of coercing a reference to a raw pointer, you can use the raw borrow",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "operators ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&raw const",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " (for ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "*const T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ") and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&raw mut",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " (for ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "*mut T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ").",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "These operators allow you to create raw pointers to fields to which you cannot",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "create a reference (without causing undefined behavior), such as an",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "unaligned field. This might be necessary if packed structs or uninitialized",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "memory is involved.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "#[derive(Debug, Default, Copy, Clone)]\n#[repr(C, packed)]\nstruct S {\n    aligned: u8,\n    unaligned: u32,\n}\nlet s = S::default();\nlet p = &raw const s.unaligned; // not allowed with coercion"
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "4. Get it from C.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "#[allow(unused_extern_crates)]\nextern crate libc;\n\nunsafe {\n    let my_num: *mut i32 = libc::malloc(size_of::<i32>()) as *mut i32;\n    if my_num.is_null() {\n        panic!(\"failed to allocate memory\");\n    }\n    libc::free(my_num as *mut core::ffi::c_void);\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Usually you wouldn't literally use ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "malloc",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "free",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " from Rust,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "but C APIs hand out a lot of pointers generally, so are a common source",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "of raw pointers in Rust.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "array",
        "kind": "primitive",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.array.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "A fixed-size array, denoted ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "[T; N]",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", for the element type, ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", and the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "non-negative compile-time constant size, ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "N",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "There are two syntactic forms for creating an array:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "A list with each element, i.e., ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "[x, y, z]",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ".",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "A repeat expression ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "[expr; N]",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " where ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "N",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " is how many times to repeat ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "expr",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " in the array. ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "expr",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " must either be:",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "list",
                        "items": [
                          {
                            "content": [
                              {
                                "type": "paragraph",
                                "spans": [
                                  {
                                    "text": "A value of a type implementing the ",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": "Copy",
                                    "style": "InlineCode",
                                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/marker/index.html?search=core%3A%3Amarker%3A%3ACopy"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": " trait",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  }
                                ]
                              }
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "content": [
                              {
                                "type": "paragraph",
                                "spans": [
                                  {
                                    "text": "A ",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": "const",
                                    "style": "InlineCode"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "text": " value",
                                    "style": "Plain"
                                  }
                                ]
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Note that ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "[expr; 0]",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is allowed, and produces an empty array.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "This will still evaluate ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "expr",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", however, and immediately drop the resulting value, so",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "be mindful of side effects.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Arrays of ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "any",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " size implement the following traits if the element type allows it:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "Copy",
                            "style": "InlineCode",
                            "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/marker/index.html?search=core%3A%3Amarker%3A%3ACopy"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
