              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let tuple: (u32, u32, u32) = (1, 2, 3);\nlet array: [u32; 3] = tuple.into();"
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Editions",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Prior to Rust 1.53, arrays did not implement ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "IntoIterator",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/iter/traits/collect/index.html?search=core%3A%3Aiter%3A%3Atraits%3A%3Acollect%3A%3AIntoIterator"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " by value, so the method call",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "array.into_iter()",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " auto-referenced into a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "slice iterator",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://docs.rs/slice/latest/slice/index.html?search=slice%3A%3Aiter"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". Right now, the old",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "behavior is preserved in the 2015 and 2018 editions of Rust for compatibility, ignoring",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "IntoIterator",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/iter/traits/collect/index.html?search=core%3A%3Aiter%3A%3Atraits%3A%3Acollect%3A%3AIntoIterator"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " by value. In the future, the behavior on the 2015 and 2018 edition",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "might be made consistent to the behavior of later editions.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "// Rust 2015 and 2018:\n\nlet array: [i32; 3] = [0; 3];\n\n// This creates a slice iterator, producing references to each value.\nfor item in array.into_iter().enumerate() {\n    let (i, x): (usize, &i32) = item;\n    println!(\"array[{i}] = {x}\");\n}\n\n// The `array_into_iter` lint suggests this change for future compatibility:\nfor item in array.iter().enumerate() {\n    let (i, x): (usize, &i32) = item;\n    println!(\"array[{i}] = {x}\");\n}\n\n// You can explicitly iterate an array by value using `IntoIterator::into_iter`\nfor item in IntoIterator::into_iter(array).enumerate() {\n    let (i, x): (usize, i32) = item;\n    println!(\"array[{i}] = {x}\");\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Starting in the 2021 edition, ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "array.into_iter()",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " uses ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "IntoIterator",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " normally to iterate",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "by value, and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "iter()",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " should be used to iterate by reference like previous editions.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "// Rust 2021:\n\nlet array: [i32; 3] = [0; 3];\n\n// This iterates by reference:\nfor item in array.iter().enumerate() {\n    let (i, x): (usize, &i32) = item;\n    println!(\"array[{i}] = {x}\");\n}\n\n// This iterates by value:\nfor item in array.into_iter().enumerate() {\n    let (i, x): (usize, i32) = item;\n    println!(\"array[{i}] = {x}\");\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Future language versions might start treating the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "array.into_iter()",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "syntax on editions 2015 and 2018 the same as on edition 2021. So code using",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "those older editions should still be written with this change in mind, to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "prevent breakage in the future. The safest way to accomplish this is to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "avoid the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "into_iter",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " syntax on those editions. If an edition update is not",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "viable/desired, there are multiple alternatives:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "use ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "iter",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ", equivalent to the old behavior, creating references",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "use ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "IntoIterator::into_iter",
                            "style": "InlineCode",
                            "url": "https://docs.rs/IntoIterator/latest/IntoIterator/index.html?search=IntoIterator%3A%3Ainto%5Fiter"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ", equivalent to the post-2021 behavior (Rust 1.53+)",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "replace ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "for ... in array.into_iter() {",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " with ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "for ... in array {",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ",",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "equivalent to the post-2021 behavior (Rust 1.53+)",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "// Rust 2015 and 2018:\n\nlet array: [i32; 3] = [0; 3];\n\n// This iterates by reference:\nfor item in array.iter() {\n    let x: &i32 = item;\n    println!(\"{x}\");\n}\n\n// This iterates by value:\nfor item in IntoIterator::into_iter(array) {\n    let x: i32 = item;\n    println!(\"{x}\");\n}\n\n// This iterates by value:\nfor item in array {\n    let x: i32 = item;\n    println!(\"{x}\");\n}\n\n// IntoIter can also start a chain.\n// This iterates by value:\nfor item in IntoIterator::into_iter(array).enumerate() {\n    let (i, x): (usize, i32) = item;\n    println!(\"array[{i}] = {x}\");\n}"
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "slice",
        "kind": "primitive",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.slice.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "A dynamically-sized view into a contiguous sequence, ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "[T]",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Contiguous here means that elements are laid out so that every element is the same",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "distance from its neighbors.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "See also the ",
                    "style": "Emphasis",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/index.html?search=alloc%3A%3Aslice"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "std::slice",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/index.html?search=alloc%3A%3Aslice"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " module",
                    "style": "Emphasis",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/index.html?search=alloc%3A%3Aslice"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Slices are a view into a block of memory represented as a pointer and a",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "length.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "// slicing a Vec\nlet vec = vec![1, 2, 3];\nlet int_slice = &vec[..];\n// coercing an array to a slice\nlet str_slice: &[&str] = &[\"one\", \"two\", \"three\"];"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Slices are either mutable or shared. The shared slice type is ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&[T]",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ",",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "while the mutable slice type is ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&mut [T]",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", where ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " represents the element",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "type. For example, you can mutate the block of memory that a mutable slice",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "points to:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let mut x = [1, 2, 3];\nlet x = &mut x[..]; // Take a full slice of `x`.\nx[1] = 7;\nassert_eq!(x, &[1, 7, 3]);"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "It is possible to slice empty subranges of slices by using empty ranges (including ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "slice.len()..slice.len()",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "):",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let x = [1, 2, 3];\nlet empty = &x[0..0];   // subslice before the first element\nassert_eq!(empty, &[]);\nlet empty = &x[..0];    // same as &x[0..0]\nassert_eq!(empty, &[]);\nlet empty = &x[1..1];   // empty subslice in the middle\nassert_eq!(empty, &[]);\nlet empty = &x[3..3];   // subslice after the last element\nassert_eq!(empty, &[]);\nlet empty = &x[3..];    // same as &x[3..3]\nassert_eq!(empty, &[]);"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "It is not allowed to use subranges that start with lower bound bigger than ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "slice.len()",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ":",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let x = vec![1, 2, 3];\nlet _ = &x[4..4];"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "As slices store the length of the sequence they refer to, they have twice",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the size of pointers to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Sized",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/index.html?search=std%3A%3ASized"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " types.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Also see the reference on",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "dynamically sized types",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/index.html?search=std%3A%3A%2E%2Freference%2Fdynamically%2Dsized%2Dtypes"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let pointer_size = size_of::<&u8>();\nassert_eq!(2 * pointer_size, size_of::<&[u8]>());\nassert_eq!(2 * pointer_size, size_of::<*const [u8]>());\nassert_eq!(2 * pointer_size, size_of::<Box<[u8]>>());\nassert_eq!(2 * pointer_size, size_of::<Rc<[u8]>>());"
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Trait Implementations",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Some traits are implemented for slices if the element type implements",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "that trait. This includes ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Eq",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cmp/index.html?search=core%3A%3Acmp%3A%3AEq"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Hash",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/hash/index.html?search=core%3A%3Ahash%3A%3AHash"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Ord",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cmp/index.html?search=core%3A%3Acmp%3A%3AOrd"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Iteration",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The slices implement ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "IntoIterator",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". The iterator yields references to the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "slice elements.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let numbers: &[i32] = &[0, 1, 2];\nfor n in numbers {\n    println!(\"{n} is a number!\");\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The mutable slice yields mutable references to the elements:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let mut scores: &mut [i32] = &mut [7, 8, 9];\nfor score in scores {\n    *score += 1;\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This iterator yields mutable references to the slice's elements, so while",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the element type of the slice is ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "i32",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", the element type of the iterator is",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&mut i32",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": ".iter",
                            "style": "InlineCode",
                            "url": "https://docs.rs/slice/latest/slice/index.html?search=slice%3A%3Aiter"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " and ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ".iter_mut",
                            "style": "InlineCode",
                            "url": "https://docs.rs/slice/latest/slice/index.html?search=slice%3A%3Aiter%5Fmut"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " are the explicit methods to return the default",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "iterators.",
