      {
        "path": "reference",
        "kind": "primitive",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.reference.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "References, ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&mut T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "A reference represents a borrow of some owned value. You can get one by using the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " or ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&mut",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "operators on a value, or by using a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "ref",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/index.html?search=std%3A%3A%2E%2Fstd%2Fkeyword%2Eref"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " or",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "ref",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/index.html?search=std%3A%3A%2E%2Fstd%2Fkeyword%2Eref"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "mut",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/index.html?search=std%3A%3A%2E%2Fstd%2Fkeyword%2Emut"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " pattern.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "For those familiar with pointers, a reference is just a pointer that is assumed to be",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "aligned, not null, and pointing to memory containing a valid value of ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " - for example,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "bool",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.bool.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " can only point to an allocation containing the integer values ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "1",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "(",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "true",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/index.html?search=std%3A%3A%2E%2Fstd%2Fkeyword%2Etrue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ") or ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "0",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " (",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "false",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/index.html?search=std%3A%3A%2E%2Fstd%2Fkeyword%2Efalse"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "), but",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "creating a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "bool",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.bool.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " that points to an allocation containing",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the value ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "3",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " causes undefined behavior.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "In fact, ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Option",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/option/index.html?search=core%3A%3Aoption%3A%3AOption"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "<&T>",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " has the same memory representation as a",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "nullable but aligned pointer, and can be passed across FFI boundaries as such.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "In most cases, references can be used much like the original value. Field access, method",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "calling, and indexing work the same (save for mutability rules, of course). In addition, the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "comparison operators transparently defer to the referent's implementation, allowing references",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "to be compared the same as owned values.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "References have a lifetime attached to them, which represents the scope for which the borrow is",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "valid. A lifetime is said to \"outlive\" another one if its representative scope is as long or",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "longer than the other. The ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "'static",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " lifetime is the longest lifetime, which represents the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "total life of the program. For example, string literals have a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "'static",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " lifetime because the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "text data is embedded into the binary of the program, rather than in an allocation that needs",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "to be dynamically managed.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "&mut T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " references can be freely coerced into ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " references with the same referent type, and",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "references with longer lifetimes can be freely coerced into references with shorter ones.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "PartialEq",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cmp/index.html?search=core%3A%3Acmp%3A%3APartialEq"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " will compare referenced values. It is possible to compare the reference address",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "using reference-pointer coercion and raw pointer equality via ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "ptr::eq",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/ptr/index.html?search=core%3A%3Aptr%3A%3Aeq"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "use std::ptr;\n\nlet five = 5;\nlet other_five = 5;\nlet five_ref = &five;\nlet same_five_ref = &five;\nlet other_five_ref = &other_five;\n\nassert!(five_ref == same_five_ref);\nassert!(five_ref == other_five_ref);\n\nassert!(ptr::eq(five_ref, same_five_ref));\nassert!(!ptr::eq(five_ref, other_five_ref));"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "For more information on how to use references, see ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the book's section on \"References and",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/index.html?search=std%3A%3A%2E%2Fbook%2Fch04%2D02%2Dreferences%2Dand%2Dborrowing"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/index.html?search=std%3A%3A%2E%2Fbook%2Fch04%2D02%2Dreferences%2Dand%2Dborrowing"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Borrowing\"",
