                    "text": "d",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/intrinsics/index.html?search=core%3A%3Aintrinsics%3A%3Atransmute"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " from the type in the declaration to the type in the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "pointer. All the usual caveats and concerns around transmutation apply; for instance, if the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "function expects a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "NonZero<i32>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and the function pointer uses the ABI-compatible type",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
